{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:42:56.762Z","ordinal":21606,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_077ca705e7ea3749016a8758bdaa34819183aad599d964583b","status":"completed","call_id":"call_dXnMiPwaZ9yWkMEHWcOdy52F","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql --paginate -F owner=21nCo -F name=super-functions -F number=115 -f query='query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!,$endCursor:String){repository(owner:$owner,name:$name){pullRequest(number:$number){headRefOid reviewThreads(first:100,after:$endCursor){nodes{id isResolved path line comments(first:20){nodes{author{login} body url createdAt}}}pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}}}' | jq -s '{head: .[0].data.repository.pullRequest.headRefOid, total: ([.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]] | length), unresolved: [.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved == false) | {id,path,line,comments}]}'`,\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/review-followup-dev-2026-08-20\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 20000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787254972.69564}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:42:59.599Z","ordinal":21607,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a020b2-bc0f-7c41-902c-9c02c407913a","call_id":"call_dXnMiPwaZ9yWkMEHWcOdy52F","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\n  \"head\": \"54b378fc529c55bb6c3a413d0ae5be2fe3b506a7\",\n  \"total\": 215,\n  \"unresolved\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a7yVA\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts\",\n      \"line\": 266,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"pullfrog\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**P1: Persist fail-closed intent before returning.** When both writes fail, this starts only an unref'd process-local timer while the durable row still says `operation: \\\"share\\\"`; process exit loses the conversion intent, and the push caller can also reconcile the still-present failed grant immediately after receiving `null`.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Make failed-share settlement durable before returning\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts:266` — the only record of the required conversion is held in `precommitLeaseHeartbeats`, while the persisted mutation remains `share`.\\n- `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/__tests__/share-spv2.test.ts:536` — the regression confirms the durable row remains `share` until the fake timer runs, but does not cover process termination.\\n- `datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts:1217` — a `null` result is still marked deferred, so the failure branch skips discard and falls through to ordinary reconciliation with no compensation task ID.\\n- `datafn/server/src/plugins/public-links.ts:738` — the nullable result is ignored, leaving the same process-death window after an incomplete compensation.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Returning from failed-share handling must leave no durable outbox row that can later execute the failed operation as `share`, even if the process terminates before another timer tick.\\n- Callers must not perform ordinary share reconciliation when durable compensation was not established.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115#discussion_r3824719467\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T19:31:38Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a74sz\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1135,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"greptile-apps\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<a href=\\\"#\\\"><img alt=\\\"P1\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"></a> **Committed share loses reconciliation**\\n\\n`executeMutationOp` commits the permission grant before `enqueuePermissionDirectorySync` persists its outbox task. When that enqueue throws, this catch records an `INTERNAL` failure and `continue`s, bypassing change tracking and directory draining. Since the outbox write itself failed, no durable task remains to reconcile the committed grant. Persist the grant and reconciliation task atomically, or record a durable compensating retry before returning a failure.\\n\\n<details><summary>Prompt To Fix With AI</summary>\\n\\n`````markdown\\nThis is a comment left during a code review.\\nPath: datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts\\nLine: 1131-1135\\n\\nComment:\\n**Committed share loses reconciliation**\\n\\n`executeMutationOp` commits the permission grant before `enqueuePermissionDirectorySync` persists its outbox task. When that enqueue throws, this catch records an `INTERNAL` failure and `continue`s, bypassing change tracking and directory draining. Since the outbox write itself failed, no durable task remains to reconcile the committed grant. Persist the grant and reconciliation task atomically, or record a durable compensating retry before returning a failure.\\n\\n---\\n\\nFor each issue above, determine whether it is valid and should be fixed. If so, fix it directly.\\n`````\\n</details>\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115#discussion_r3824758470\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T19:37:34Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a74s3\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1190,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"greptile-apps\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<a href=\\\"#\\\"><img alt=\\\"P1\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"></a> **Post-commit drain masks success**\\n\\nWhen a multi-region share commits and the subsequent outbox lookup or retry-state update rejects, this unguarded drain exits before `recordMutationSuccess`, causing the push endpoint to return `INTERNAL` without storing the successful mutation ID. A client retry can then re-execute the already-committed share; the same ordering occurs in the non-transactional success path.\\n\\n<details><summary>Prompt To Fix With AI</summary>\\n\\n`````markdown\\nThis is a comment left during a code review.\\nPath: datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts\\nLine: 1189-1190\\n\\nComment:\\n**Post-commit drain masks success**\\n\\nWhen a multi-region share commits and the subsequent outbox lookup or retry-state update rejects, this unguarded drain exits before `recordMutationSuccess`, causing the push endpoint to return `INTERNAL` without storing the successful mutation ID. A client retry can then re-execute the already-committed share; the same ordering occurs in the non-transactional success path.\\n\\n---\\n\\nFor each issue above, determine whether it is valid and should be fixed. If so, fix it directly.\\n`````\\n</details>\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115#discussion_r3824758476\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T19:37:34Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a74s6\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/execute.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1163,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"greptile-apps\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<a href=\\\"#\\\"><img alt=\\\"P1\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"></a> <a href=\\\"#\\\"><img alt=\\\"security\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Security.svg?v=2\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"></a> **Rollback publishes uncommitted permission state**\\n\\nWhen an earlier step changes a permission grant and a later step fails in the same atomic transaction, this branch reconciles through the still-open transaction adapter before the enclosing rollback settles, causing the external directory to advertise a grant that the database subsequently rolls back. If the settled-state drain then fails, the unauthorized grant remains advertised until the durable retry runs.\\n\\n**How this was verified:** The transaction passes its adapter into `executeMutation`, which invokes this reconciliation before the outer rollback and settled-state drain.\\n\\n<details><summary>Prompt To Fix With AI</summary>\\n\\n`````markdown\\nThis is a comment left during a code review.\\nPath: datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/execute.ts\\nLine: 1147-1163\\n\\nComment:\\n**Rollback publishes uncommitted permission state**\\n\\nWhen an earlier step changes a permission grant and a later step fails in the same atomic transaction, this branch reconciles through the still-open transaction adapter before the enclosing rollback settles, causing the external directory to advertise a grant that the database subsequently rolls back. If the settled-state drain then fails, the unauthorized grant remains advertised until the durable retry runs.\\n\\n**How this was verified:** The transaction passes its adapter into `executeMutation`, which invokes this reconciliation before the outer rollback and settled-state drain.\\n\\n---\\n\\nFor each issue above, determine whether it is valid and should be fixed. If so, fix it directly.\\n`````\\n</details>\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115#discussion_r3824758480\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T19:37:34Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a7958\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1226,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"cubic-dev-ai\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=41b858b3-2ada-42d8-983e-70bc57c79922 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=b8ff641b-51a8-43fc-a743-8c634c925ade -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP1: When compensation persistence returns `null`, this flag still routes the failed share into reconciliation. With no task ID, `reconcilePermissionDirectoryAfterSettlement` directly indexes the original share, exposing a partial grant instead of leaving it pending for fail-closed conversion. Skip the original-share reconciliation when no compensation task was returned, while retaining the leased retry task.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts, line 1226:\\n\\n<comment>When compensation persistence returns `null`, this flag still routes the failed share into reconciliation. With no task ID, `reconcilePermissionDirectoryAfterSettlement` directly indexes the original share, exposing a partial grant instead of leaving it pending for fail-closed conversion. Skip the original-share reconciliation when no compensation task was returned, while retaining the leased retry task.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -1214,25 +1214,16 @@ export async function executePush(\\n+            namespace,\\n+            multiRegionRuntime.regionId,\\n+          );\\n+          failedShareCompensationDeferred = true;\\n         }\\n         logger?.error(\\\"Push operation failed\\\", { error: String(error), operation: mut.operation, resource: mut.resource, id: mut.id });\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115#discussion_r3824792212\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T19:41:45Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a795_\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts\",\n      \"line\": 251,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"cubic-dev-ai\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=b15d6276-d0e7-48be-b494-6da6528d6dc9 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=b8ff641b-51a8-43fc-a743-8c634c925ade -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When the conditional delete returns 0 because another drainer claimed or deleted the row, this starts a settlement heartbeat that can never match `expectedLeaseValue`. It retries every second forever after the row disappears, retaining an entry in `precommitLeaseHeartbeats` and issuing continuous outbox updates; stop the heartbeat on ownership loss instead of starting it for a zero delete result.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts, line 251:\\n\\n<comment>When the conditional delete returns 0 because another drainer claimed or deleted the row, this starts a settlement heartbeat that can never match `expectedLeaseValue`. It retries every second forever after the row disappears, retaining an entry in `precommitLeaseHeartbeats` and issuing continuous outbox updates; stop the heartbeat on ownership loss instead of starting it for a zero delete result.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -183,33 +203,72 @@ export async function deferFailedShareCompensation(\\n+          { field: \\\"next_attempt_at\\\", op: \\\"eq\\\", value: expectedLeaseValue },\\n+        ]);\\n+        if (deleted === 0) {\\n+          startPrecommitLeaseHeartbeat(db, taskId, expectedLeaseValue, {\\n+            mutation: serializedMutation,\\n+            lastError,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115#discussion_r3824792218\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T19:41:45Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787254979.599512}}}
