{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:45:02.585Z","ordinal":21686,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"item-1179","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The core fail-closed redesign now waits for a persisted compensation task and conditionally removes any still-runnable original share row before returning—there is no process-local “success later” state or nullable task result. I also routed guard-failure reconciliation through the outer transaction’s settlement deferral. Existing tests already prove transactional outbox failure rolls back the grant and post-commit drain errors preserve success; I’m re-running those focused suites now."}],"phase":"commentary"},"completed_at_ms":1787255102585}}
