{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:45:49.687Z","ordinal":21707,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_077ca705e7ea3749016a87596174688191b907cc4f3f9b0235","status":"completed","call_id":"call_uY1kQmQ2GqXoLdl4pLpH7FTN","name":"exec","input":"const cwd = \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/review-followup-dev-2026-08-20\";\nconst env = \"GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other\";\nconst replies = [\n  {\n    id: \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a7yVA\",\n    body: \"Fixed in 6c440675. Failed-share handling no longer returns a nullable/process-local retry state. It waits until a compensation task is durably created (or the owned task is durably rewritten), then repeatedly reads and conditionally removes any remaining original row while it is still runnable as share. The regression now proves the promise remains unsettled during an outbox outage and returns only after every durable survivor is compensation work. DataFn Server: 961 passing, 1 skipped; typecheck/build green.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a7958\",\n    body: \"Fixed in 6c440675. deferFailedShareCompensation now returns a durable task ID, never null: it does not return until replacement compensation is persisted and no durable original row remains runnable as share. The push caller therefore reconciles compensation work, not the failed original share. The outage regression covers the prior nullable window. DataFn Server: 961 passing, 1 skipped; typecheck/build green.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a795_\",\n    body: \"Fixed in 6c440675. The process-local settlement heartbeat path was removed entirely. On ownership loss, a durable replacement compensation task is created and the original row is re-read/conditionally removed; a zero conditional delete causes a re-read, not an unbounded stale heartbeat. DataFn Server: 961 passing, 1 skipped; typecheck/build green.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a74sz\",\n    body: \"Verified this path is already atomic and covered. The share and enqueue at push.ts:1121-1135 both execute inside the same db.transaction callback using txDb; an enqueue throw aborts that callback and rolls back the grant. The regression \\\"rolls back a transactional push share when its outbox write fails\\\" forces this exact failure and asserts no canonical grant, no directory entry, and no outbox task. It passes in the full 961-test server suite, so no product change is warranted for this thread.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a74s3\",\n    body: \"Verified the alleged masking path is already fenced. reconcilePermissionDirectoryAfterSettlement catches both drainPermissionDirectorySync rejection and direct sync rejection, logs them, and returns; recordMutationSuccess then executes. The regression \\\"keeps a committed push share successful when immediate outbox draining throws\\\" forces the outbox read failure and asserts the mutation remains applied/idempotent with its durable retry task. It passes in the full 961-test server suite.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a74s6\",\n    body: \"The share rollback scenario is already deferred to the settled outer adapter: insideTransaction routes reconciliation callbacks into executeTransaction, which invokes them only after commit/rollback. The regression \\\"does not publish a share from an outer transaction that rolls back\\\" asserts zero directory put calls, no canonical grant, and no indexed record, and passes. 6c440675 additionally routes the guard-mismatch task path through the same settlement deferral instead of calling the transaction adapter directly. DataFn Server: 961 passing, 1 skipped; typecheck/build green.\"\n  }\n];\nfor (const item of replies) {\n  const reply = await tools.exec_command({\n    cmd: `${env} gh api graphql -F threadId='${item.id}' -F body=${JSON.stringify(item.body)} -f query='mutation($threadId:ID!,$body:String!){addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(input:{pullRequestReviewThreadId:$threadId,body:$body}){comment{id url}}}'`,\n    workdir: cwd,\n    yield_time_ms: 10000,\n    max_output_tokens: 6000\n  });\n  text(`reply ${item.id}: exit=${reply.exit_code}\\n${reply.output}`);\n  if (reply.exit_code !== 0) continue;\n  const resolve = await tools.exec_command({\n    cmd: `${env} gh api graphql -F threadId='${item.id}' -f query='mutation($threadId:ID!){resolveReviewThread(input:{threadId:$threadId}){thread{id isResolved}}}'`,\n    workdir: cwd,\n    yield_time_ms: 10000,\n    max_output_tokens: 6000\n  });\n  text(`resolve ${item.id}: exit=${resolve.exit_code}\\n${resolve.output}`);\n}\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787255135.527366}}}
