{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:53:17.848Z","ordinal":21777,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_077ca705e7ea3749016a875b2abfa08191889f838d3edd3a3a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_sB0EyB2KYk7lNG0e1woJ86nY","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql --paginate -F owner=21nCo -F name=super-functions -F number=115 -f query='query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!,$endCursor:String){repository(owner:$owner,name:$name){pullRequest(number:$number){headRefOid reviewThreads(first:100,after:$endCursor){nodes{id isResolved path line comments(first:20){nodes{author{login} body url createdAt}}}pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}}}' | jq -s '{head: .[0].data.repository.pullRequest.headRefOid, total: ([.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]] | length), unresolved: [.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved == false) | {id,path,line,comments}]}'`,\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/review-followup-dev-2026-08-20\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 22000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787255593.794301}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T19:53:20.614Z","ordinal":21778,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a020bc-35e6-7753-bf94-1328f492ffc1","call_id":"call_sB0EyB2KYk7lNG0e1woJ86nY","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\n  \"head\": \"6c44067506c0133cbf48b02ea9888bbb717f78be\",\n  \"total\": 217,\n  \"unresolved\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a8FnW\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/execute.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1527,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile failed shares when task ownership is lost**\\n\\nWhen a nontransactional share outlives its precommit lease (for example, heartbeat renewal is delayed), a drainer can claim the task and publish the partially written canonical grant before the legacy mirror fails and local rollback succeeds. Fresh evidence beyond the earlier failed-share fix is that `discardPermissionDirectorySync()` now reports this ownership loss as `false`, but this result is ignored and the task ID is cleared, so no reconciliation removes the externally published grant; the push path has the same pattern. On a false discard, enqueue a replacement reconciliation against the rolled-back authoritative state instead of treating the task as gone.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115#discussion_r3824839083\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T19:48:53Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a8JPW\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts\",\n      \"line\": 227,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"pullfrog\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**P1: Back off persistent settlement retries.** This repeats every failed persistence attempt after 25 ms forever, with no cancellation or shared gate, so each failed share adds roughly 40 adapter calls per second for the process lifetime during an outage. Keep the fail-closed blocking guarantee, but add bounded exponential backoff or equivalent retry-pressure control across all three retry sites.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Bound failed-share settlement retry pressure\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts:215-228` — replacement-task creation retries every 25 ms indefinitely.\\n- `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts:234-265` — original-task reads and conditional deletes use the same unbounded cadence.\\n- `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/execute.ts:1516-1524` — request handling awaits this promise without an abort or lifecycle signal.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Preserve the rule that failed-share handling cannot return while durable `share` work remains runnable.\\n- Prevent persistent adapter failures and concurrent failed shares from generating an unbounded high-frequency retry storm.\\n\\n## Suggested approach\\n- Apply capped exponential backoff with jitter across persistence, read, and delete retries; coalesce settlement by task ID if concurrent ownership is possible.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115#discussion_r3824861122\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T19:52:18Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787255600.614124}}}
