{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T20:02:10.674Z","ordinal":22062,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"item-1199","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"After tracing the exact code, both Cubic items are non-actionable as written:\n\n- The line-1398 guard branch cannot hold a nontransactional share task; share prequeue happens later. The real failed-share discard branch was the one fixed and regression-tested in `6c4428bd`.\n- A bounded cutoff while the only durable store is unavailable would discard the compensation intent and recreate the security bug. The safe behavior is intentionally fail-closed until durable persistence succeeds; the new capped exponential backoff addresses the resource-pressure concern without weakening that invariant.\n\nI’ll document that reasoning on the threads and resolve them, then evaluate only feedback generated against the new head."}],"phase":"commentary"},"completed_at_ms":1787256130674}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T20:02:10.674Z","ordinal":22063,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_077ca705e7ea3749016a875d40a0948191b87ebcd693c6a1e4","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"After tracing the exact code, both Cubic items are non-actionable as written:\n\n- The line-1398 guard branch cannot hold a nontransactional share task; share prequeue happens later. The real failed-share discard branch was the one fixed and regression-tested in `6c4428bd`.\n- A bounded cutoff while the only durable store is unavailable would discard the compensation intent and recreate the security bug. The safe behavior is intentionally fail-closed until durable persistence succeeds; the new capped exponential backoff addresses the resource-pressure concern without weakening that invariant.\n\nI’ll document that reasoning on the threads and resolve them, then evaluate only feedback generated against the new head."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T20:02:17.154Z","ordinal":22064,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_077ca705e7ea3749016a875d42a234819198677bb7398032ed","status":"completed","call_id":"call_AwV5SKV58MCgieFVM5pO7gcz","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql -F threadId=REDACTED -f body='This is a duplicate/outdated location rather than a remaining bug. The line-1398 nontransactional guard branch cannot hold a share precommit task: nontransactional share prequeue occurs later, immediately before executeMutationCore; the only tasks prequeued into that branch are unshare tasks. The actual failed nontransactional share discard path is at the post-operation settlement block and is fixed in 6c4428bd: false discard now durably enqueues replacement reconciliation in both direct and push paths, with an ownership-loss regression that publishes then removes the partial grant.' -f query='mutation($threadId:ID!,$body:String!){addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(input:{pullRequestReviewThreadId:$threadId,body:$body}){comment{id url}}}' && GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql -F threadId=REDACTED -f query='mutation($threadId:ID!){resolveReviewThread(input:{threadId:$threadId}){thread{id isResolved}}}' && GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql -F threadId=REDACTED -f body='A bounded cutoff is not safe here: while the outbox is unavailable there is no independent durable handoff target, so returning/cancelling would lose the failed-share compensation intent and permit the original task to publish partial grant state. This path is deliberately fail-closed until the intent is durable. Commit 6c4428bd addresses the actionable resource-pressure issue with capped exponential retry (50 ms to 5 s) and regression coverage; it intentionally does not add a deadline that weakens the security invariant. A truly bounded handoff would require a separately available durable queue, which is outside this storage contract.' -f query='mutation($threadId:ID!,$body:String!){addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(input:{pullRequestReviewThreadId:$threadId,body:$body}){comment{id url}}}' && GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql -F threadId=REDACTED -f query='mutation($threadId:ID!){resolveReviewThread(input:{threadId:$threadId}){thread{id isResolved}}}'\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/review-followup-dev-2026-08-20\",\n  yield_time_ms: 30000,\n  max_output_tokens: 12000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787256118.011057}}}
