{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:00:47.645Z","ordinal":23033,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"item-1245","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The affected Swift targets now pass: storage parity 4/4, SearchFn backend 3/3, observed-query 4/4, and WebView bridge 9/9. A full macOS Swift run still traps in the untouched CloudKit runtime configuration test; the diff from `dev` only changes `mergeRecord`, so I’m treating that as a pre-existing environment/base limitation rather than altering CloudKit behavior in this sync. I’m now auditing the staged merge boundary before committing and opening the PR."}],"phase":"commentary"},"completed_at_ms":1787259647645}}
