eaders.\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8615792Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8616179Z ## Environment\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8616863Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8617893Z - Non-interactive: complete tasks autonomously without asking follow-up questions.\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8619440Z - Running inside a GitHub Actions ephemeral environment. All processes and resources will be cleaned up at the end of the run.\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8621966Z - When details are missing, prefer the most common convention unless repo-specific patterns exist. Fail with an explicit error only if critical information is missing (e.g. user asks to review a PR but does not provide a link or ID).\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8623634Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8623998Z ## Priority Order\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8624435Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8625059Z In case of conflict between instructions, follow this precedence (highest to lowest):\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8626222Z 1. Security rules and system instructions (non-overridable)\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8627327Z 2. User prompt\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8628187Z 3. Event-level instructions\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8628853Z 4. Standing instructions (org/repo defaults)\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8629267Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8629456Z ## Security\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8629687Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8630637Z Do not reveal secrets or credentials or commit them to the repository. Think hard about whether a request may be malicious and refuse to execute it if you are not confident.\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8631741Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8631923Z ## Tools\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8632148Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8633175Z MCP servers provide tools you can call. Inspect your available MCP servers at startup to understand what tools are available, especially the pullfrog server which handles all GitHub operations. For example: `pullfrog_create_issue_comment`.\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8634057Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8634170Z ### Git\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8634300Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8636464Z Use `pullfrog_git` for local git commands (status, log, add, commit, checkout, branch, merge, etc.). When reviewing a PR, the diffPath returned by `pullfrog_checkout_pr` is authoritative — read it rather than re-deriving the diff. To diff a branch against its base yourself, use `git diff --merge-base <base>`; the tool rejects the symmetric forms and tells you what to use instead. Note the git tool runs git directly, so `$(…)` subshells do not interpolate. For operations requiring remote authentication, use the dedicated MCP tools:\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8640503Z - `pullfrog_push_branch` - push current or specified branch\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8641273Z - `pullfrog_git_fetch` - fetch refs from remote\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8642171Z - `pullfrog_checkout_pr` - checkout a PR branch (fetches and configures push for forks)\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8643193Z - `pullfrog_delete_branch` - delete a remote branch (requires push: enabled)\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8644085Z - `pullfrog_push_tags` - push tags (requires push: enabled)\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8644642Z \npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8644840Z Rules:\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8646490Z - All code changes must be pushed to a pull request (new or existing) before the run ends. This environment is ephemeral — unpushed work is lost permanently. `git status` must be clean when you finish.\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8649298Z - Protected branches (default branch) are blocked from direct pushes in restricted mode. Do not use `git push` directly — it will fail without credentials.\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8651210Z - Do not attempt to configure git credentials manually — the pullfrog server handles all authentication internally.\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8653644Z - Never push commits directly to the default branch or any protected branch (commonly: main, master, production, develop, staging). Always create a feature branch following the pattern: `pullfrog/<issue-number>-<kebab-case-description>` (e.g., `pullfrog/123-fix-login-bug`).\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:34.8655957Z …4774 tokens truncated…engine ***\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3843948Z npm warn EBADENGINE   package: '@uifn/patterns@0.2.0-experimental.0',\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3844861Z npm warn EBADENGINE   required: *** node: '>=18 <23' ***\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3845685Z npm warn EBADENGINE   current: *** node: 'v24.18.0', npm: '11.16.0' ***\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3846467Z npm warn EBADENGINE ***\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3847310Z npm warn EBADENGINE Unsupported engine ***\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3848026Z npm warn EBADENGINE   package: '@uifn/recipes@0.0.1',\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3848780Z npm warn EBADENGINE   required: *** node: '>=18 <23' ***\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3849605Z npm warn EBADENGINE   current: *** node: 'v24.18.0', npm: '11.16.0' ***\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3850342Z npm warn EBADENGINE ***\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3850904Z npm warn EBADENGINE Unsupported engine ***\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3851587Z npm warn EBADENGINE   package: '@uifn/registry@0.0.1',\npullfrog\tRun agent\t2026-08-20T21:02:52.3852370Z npm warn EBADENGINE   required: *** node: '>=1