{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:07:36.440Z","ordinal":23141,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"item-1254","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Guardrails failed on its existing LangFn policy check, not on any changed file: the script requires finding `@superfunctions/` or `superfunctions.` usage under LangFn, and `rg` returns no match. The duplication rate itself is only 2.13%, below its 5% threshold. I’m checking the same workflow on the untouched `next` base to confirm whether this is inherited before deciding whether any in-scope action is warranted."}],"phase":"commentary"},"completed_at_ms":1787260056440}}
