{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:14:49.736Z","ordinal":23228,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a02106-d008-70e2-a1b0-79cc1ef328ca","call_id":"call_7hT16GmlWrWQvr7hkofiVCjo","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\n  \"head\": \"dd612cdd2ffec0b169465c9508f534b2c68ff015\",\n  \"total\": 1,\n  \"unresolved\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9c5z\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1185,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile an aborted unshare before recording its failure**\\n\\nWhen a transactional `unshare` aborts after invalidating the external directory, `recordMutationFailure()` can itself reject while writing the idempotency result. Because reconciliation runs afterward, that rejection skips this call entirely: the database rollback restores the grant, while the prequeued task's heartbeat continues renewing its lease and prevents the background drainer from restoring the directory entry until the process restarts. Run the reconciliation in a `finally` block or before the fallible failure-recording write.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825369878\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T21:09:37Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787260489.736245}}}
