b-store.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/internal-tables.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/__tests__/share-spv2.test.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/execute.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/relations.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/share.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/query/aggregate.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/query/filters.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/query/planner.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/query/select.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/relations/inheritance.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/sync/clone.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/sync/reconcile.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/sync/resource-id.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/execution/transact.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/plugins/multi-region.test.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/plugins/multi-region.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/plugins/public-links.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/routes/query.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/server.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/validation/__tests__/validation.test.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/validation/query.ts`\\n* `datafn/server/src/validation/schema.ts`\\n* `datafn/swift-bridge/README.md`\\n* `datafn/swift-bridge/__tests__/nativeRemote.test.ts`\\n* `datafn/swift-bridge/__tests__/nativeStorage.test.ts`\\n* `datafn/swift-bridge/__tests__/nativeSyncController.test.ts`\\n* `datafn/swift-bridge/src/index.ts`\\n* `datafn/swift-bridge/src/nativeStorage.ts`\\n* `datafn/swift-bridge/src/nativeSyncController.ts`\\n* `datafn/swift-bridge/src/protocol.ts`\\n* `datafn/swift/Sources/DatafnCoreDataStore/DatafnCoreDataStore.swift`\\n* `datafn/swift/Sources/DatafnWebViewBridgeHost/DatafnBridgeDispatcher.swift`\\n* `datafn/swift/Tests/DatafnCoreDataStoreTests/StorageParityTests.swift`\\n* `datafn/swift/Tests/DatafnSearchFnBackendTests/DatafnSearchFnBackendTests.swift`\\n* `datafn/swift/Tests/DatafnSwiftUITests/ObservedQueryTests.swift`\\n* `datafn/swift/Tests/DatafnWebViewBridgeHostTests/BridgeHostTests.swift`\\n* `packages/cli/src/__tests__/schema-index-migrations.test.ts`\\n* `packages/cli/src/commands/generate-schema.ts`\\n* `packages/cli/src/utils/generators.ts`\\n* `packages/cli/src/utils/introspection.ts`\\n* `packages/cli/src/utils/mysql-types.ts`\\n* `packages/cli/src/utils/schema-diff.ts`\\n* `packages/cli/src/utils/schema-generators.ts`\\n* `packages/db/src/adapter/types.ts`\\n* `packages/db/src/adapters/dynamodb/index.test.ts`\\n* `packages/db/src/adapters/dynamodb/index.ts`\\n* `packages/observability/src/index.test.ts`\\n* `packages/observability/src/index.ts`\\n* `packages/observability/vitest.config.ts`\\n* `plugfn/core/src/core/plug-fn.ts`\\n* `plugfn/core/src/schema.ts`\\n* `plugfn/core/src/storage/adapters/database.ts`\\n* `plugfn/core/tests/schema.test.ts`\\n* `plugfn/core/tests/sync-runtime.test.ts`\\n* `searchfn/datafn-provider/__tests__/factory.test.ts`\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n**Included review availability:** Your plan provides up to 1 included review per hour; 0 remain after this review.\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- recent_review_end --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- walkthrough_start --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e📝 Walkthrough\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n## Walkthrough\\n\\nThis PR updates rate limiting, storage merge semantics, relation compatibility, permission-directory reconciliation, schema migration generation, bridge capability negotiation, synchronization retries, and several adapter and test behaviors across AuthFn, Datafn, PlugFn, SearchFn, and supporting packages.\\n\\n### Changes\\n\\n**AuthFn runtime and rate-limit updates**\\n\\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\\n|---|---|\\n|**Runtime test and rate-limit behavior** \\u003cbr\\u003e `authfn/core/src/core/rate-limit.ts`, `authfn/core/src/__tests__/*`, `authfn/social-oauth/*`|Rate-limit state is isolated per middleware instance. Active windows are not evicted at capacity. AuthFn tests use runtime server helpers.|\\n|**Two-factor key validation** \\u003cbr\\u003e `authfn/examples/account-settings/server/src/index.ts`, `authfn/examples/account-settings/README.md`|Two-factor keys accept normalized padded or unpadded base64 and must decode to 32 bytes.|\\n\\n**Datafn client storage and synchronization**\\n\\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\\n|---|---|\\n|**Atomic storage merge contract** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/client/src/storage.ts`, `datafn/client/src/adapters/*`, `datafn/docs/content/docs/documentation/storage/*`, `datafn/swift/*`|Adapters advertise atomic missing-record merge support. `mergeRecord` accepts `options.ifMissing` for creation.|\\n|**Offline mutation and relation handling** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/client/src/offline/*`, `datafn/client/__tests__/*`|Offline merges use atomic creation when supported. Relation resolution accepts the legacy `foreignKey` alias.|\\n|**Query overlays and encryption scope** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/client/src/query.ts`, `datafn/client/src/e2ee.ts`, `datafn/client/src/__tests__/*`|Offset-zero and equivalent queries retain local overlays. Envelope reuse is scoped by provider and key reference.|\\n|**Compacted mutation replay** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/client/src/sync/engine.ts`, `datafn/client/src/sync/__tests__/engine.test.ts`|Compacted writes are selectively resent when replacing deletes fail.|\\n\\n**Datafn schema and relation compatibility**\\n\\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\\n|---|---|\\n|**Schema and relation contracts** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/core/src/schema.ts`, `datafn/core/src/types.ts`, `datafn/core/src/sort.ts`, `datafn/core/__tests__/*`|Schemas validate relation aliases, normalized resource prefixes, and explicit null sort directions.|\\n|**Legacy relation-key resolution** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/core/src/relation-fks.ts`, `datafn/cli/src/codegen.ts`, `datafn/cli/src/drizzle-codegen.ts`, `datafn/cli/__tests__/*`|Relation code generation and core resolution use `foreignKey` before derived defaults.|\\n\\n**Datafn server permission-directory and query execution**\\n\\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\\n|---|---|\\n|**Permission-directory outbox** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/server/src/execution/internal-tables.ts`, `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts`, `datafn/server/src/execution/transact.ts`|The server persists, leases, drains, retries, and settles permission-directory tasks across transaction boundaries.|\\n|**Share compensation and mutation wiring** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/{share,execute}.ts`, `datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts`, `datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/__tests__/share-spv2.test.ts`|Share failures capture prior grants, restore state, and coordinate durable directory repair.|\\n|**Regional directory lifecycle** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/server/src/plugins/{multi-region,public-links}.ts`, `datafn/server/src/server.ts`, `datafn/server/__tests__/*`|Regional runtimes are validated and drained at startup and during retries. Permission reads and legacy keys are region-aware.|\\n|**Query and relation execution** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/server/src/execution/{db-store,query,relations}/*`, `datafn/server/src/validation/*`|Server query and mutation paths support legacy relation keys and validate falsy temporal and null-check inputs.|\\n|**Resource ID and reconciliation** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/server/src/execution/sync/{resource-id,reconcile,clone}.ts`|Resource matching uses configured prefixes and reconciliation falls back when direct join counts fail.|\\n\\n**Swift storage capability negotiation**\\n\\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\\n|---|---|\\n|**Bridge capability negotiation** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/swift-bridge/src/*`, `datafn/swift-bridge/__tests__/*`|The bridge negotiates atomic merge capability with generation-aware handshakes and rejects stale results.|\\n|**Native ifMissing propagation** \\u003cbr\\u003e `datafn/swift/Sources/*`, `datafn/swift/Tests/*`|Native storage forwards and persists complete `ifMissing` creation payloads.|\\n\\n**CLI schema introspection and migration generation**\\n\\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\\n|---|---|\\n|**Introspection and schema metadata** \\u003cbr\\u003e `packages/cli/src/utils/introspection.ts`, `packages/db/src/adapter/types.ts`|Introspection records dialect-specific column, index, schema, and constraint metadata. Fields support `maxLength`.|\\n|**MySQL type and index validation** \\u003cbr\\u003e `packages/cli/src/utils/mysql-types.ts`, `packages/cli/src/utils/schema-diff.ts`|MySQL string lengths, metadata syntax, index limits, and dependency changes are validated.|\\n|**Dialect-aware migration generation** \\u003cbr\\u003e `packages/cli/src/utils/generators.ts`, `packages/cli/src/utils/schema-generators.ts`|Generators preserve MySQL metadata, rebuild indexes, emit dialect-specific SQL, and create rollback operations.|\\n|**Migration regression coverage** \\u003cbr\\u003e `packages/cli/src/__tests__/schema-index-migrations.test.ts`|Tests cover introspection, MySQL constraints, index changes, generated SQL, and rollback ordering.|\\n\\n**Package reliability updates**\\n\\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\\n|---|---|\\n|**Adapter and observability behavior** \\u003cbr\\u003e `packages/db/src/adapters/dynamodb/*`, `packages/observability/src/*`|Directory reads use strong consistency. Instrumented methods safely assimilate thenables.|\\n|**Sync-job claim tokens** \\u003cbr\\u003e `plugfn/core/src/*`, `plugfn/core/tests/*`|Sync jobs use random hexadecimal claim tokens with a maximum length and unique index.|\\n|**Search adapter filtering** \\u003cbr\\u003e `searchfn/datafn-provider/__tests__/factory.test.ts`|Unsupported metadata filters are rejected. Supported namespace and region filters are forwarded.|\\n|**OAuth test environment** \\u003cbr\\u003e `authfn/social-oauth/src/oauth-support.test.ts`, `authfn/social-oauth/vitest.config.ts`|OAuth diagnostics include successful responses, and tests use the Node environment.|\\n\\n**Estimated code review effort:** 5 (Critical) | ~120 minutes\\n\\n\\u003c!-- final_review_risk_start --\\u003e\\n**Merge Risk:** _⚪ Minimal_ · up to `dd612`\\n\\nThe PR syncs the final development state and updates auth, storage, server, CLI, Swift, and provider behavior, with the listed affected suites and builds passing; no actionable merge-blocking risk remains beyond normal checks and review.\\n\\u003c!-- final_review_risk_end --\\u003e\\n\\n### Sequence Diagram(s)\\n\\n```mermaid\\nsequenceDiagram\\n  participant Client\\n  participant NativeSyncController\\n  participant NativeHost\\n  participant NativeStorage\\n  Client-\\u003e\\u003eNativeSyncController: start handshake\\n  NativeSyncController-\\u003e\\u003eNativeHost: request capabilities\\n  NativeHost--\\u003e\\u003eNativeSyncController: return capability list\\n  NativeSyncController-\\u003e\\u003eNativeStorage: update negotiated capabilities\\n  Client-\\u003e\\u003eNativeStorage: mergeRecord with ifMissing\\n  NativeStorage-\\u003e\\u003eNativeHost: forward merge request\\n  NativeHost--\\u003e\\u003eNativeStorage: return created record\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- walkthrough_end --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- tips_start --\\u003e\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\u003e [!NOTE]\\n\\u003e \\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003csummary\\u003e🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting \\u003chttps://app.coderabbit.ai/login\\u003e.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003csub\\u003eComment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- tips_end --\\u003e\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-20T21:01:41Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.