{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:38:49.453Z","ordinal":23728,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0211c-c7ed-7160-bf6e-d9011cfed61d","call_id":"call_2x59dgEnkeDMDVmyl8pMnRYh","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e2161e\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.094254125,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3962,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"ffa358eb0b2198cbad658bafee8822b849a4c4ae\\\",\\n  \\\"total\\\": 10,\\n  \\\"unresolved\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0D\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"datafn/server/src/plugins/public-links.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 765,\\n      \\\"comment\\\": {\\n        \\\"author\\\": {\\n          \\\"login\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=cc916414-fe59-47ad-97f6-f93b5946a08c -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=3775059c-56d5-4810-9e66-69dd9a699541 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":9} -->\\\\nP1: When this rollback delete fails, the public-link row remains active and its token still authorizes queries despite the share failure. Make token invalidation durable or retry cleanup before returning the failure.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/server/src/plugins/public-links.ts, line 762:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>When this rollback delete fails, the public-link row remains active and its token still authorizes queries despite the share failure. Make token invalidation durable or retry cleanup before returning the failure.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -602,50 +628,184 @@ async function createDatafnPublicLink(input: {\\\\n+      // The public-link row is created before its permission grant. If grant\\\\n+      // creation throws, roll the token back just as we do for an explicit\\\\n+      // unsuccessful result so it can never resolve without authority.\\\\n+      await input.database.delete({\\\\n+        model: input.modelName,\\\\n+        where: [{ field: \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\", operator: \\\\\\\"eq\\\\\\\", value: id }],\\\\n</file context>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\",\\n        \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825497596\\\",\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-20T21:29:12Z\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0J\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"datafn/server/src/routes/query.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 360,\\n      \\\"comment\\\": {\\n        \\\"author\\\": {\\n          \\\"login\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=9a2634f5-be7d-48d9-9e91-ae0b467d01a3 -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=3775059c-56d5-4810-9e66-69dd9a699541 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":8} -->\\\\nP1: When the directory lookup falls back to raw database rows, a foreign-region grant stored as `resource_region` is treated as unscoped because normalization never copies that field. Normalize `resource_region` to `resourceRegion` or check both names before allowing the row.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/server/src/routes/query.ts, line 359:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>When the directory lookup falls back to raw database rows, a foreign-region grant stored as `resource_region` is treated as unscoped because normalization never copies that field. Normalize `resource_region` to `resourceRegion` or check both names before allowing the row.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -353,7 +353,14 @@ export function createQueryHandler(\\\\n+      return multiRegionRuntime\\\\n+        ? rows.filter(\\\\n+            (row) =>\\\\n+              row.resourceRegion === undefined ||\\\\n+              row.resourceRegion === null ||\\\\n+              row.resourceRegion === multiRegionRuntime.regionId,\\\\n</file context>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\",\\n        \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825497602\\\",\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-20T21:29:12Z\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0N\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"datafn/server/src/validation/schema.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": null,\\n      \\\"comment\\\": {\\n        \\\"author\\\": {\\n          \\\"login\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=5f47d406-9b22-48db-b391-275e860ba12f -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=3775059c-56d5-4810-9e66-69dd9a699541 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":9} -->\\\\nP2: When a valid many-one relation omits `relation` and declares no FK alias, this index registers `undefinedId`, while runtime relation handling uses `${firstEndpoint(to)}Id`; writes using the generated FK are therefore rejected. Use the target-resource fallback here so validation and execution derive the same field.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/server/src/validation/schema.ts, line 122:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>When a valid many-one relation omits `relation` and declares no FK alias, this index registers `undefinedId`, while runtime relation handling uses `${firstEndpoint(to)}Id`; writes using the generated FK are therefore rejected. Use the target-resource fallback here so validation and execution derive the same field.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ export function buildSchemaIndex(schema: DatafnSchema): SchemaIndex {\\\\n         const fromResources = Array.isArray(rel.from) ? rel.from : [rel.from];\\\\n         for (const fromRes of fromResources) {\\\\n-          const fkField = (rel as any).fkField ?? `${rel.relation}Id`;\\\\n+          const fkField = (rel as any).fkField || (rel as any).foreignKey || `${rel.relation}Id`;\\\\n           fieldsByResource.get(fromRes)?.add(fkField);\\\\n           writableFieldsByResource.get(fromRes)?.add(fkField);\\\\n</file context>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\\n\\\\n```suggestion\\\\n          const fkField = (rel as any).fkField || (rel as any).foreignKey || `${(rel as any).relation ?? (Array.isArray(rel.to) ? rel.to[0] : rel.to)}Id`;\\\\n```\\\",\\n        \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825497607\\\",\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-20T21:29:12Z\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0Q\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1294,\\n      \\\"comment\\\": {\\n        \\\"author\\\": {\\n          \\\"login\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=4e68b288-a88e-4b5b-9633-0f704dcdefe6 -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=3775059c-56d5-4810-9e66-69dd9a699541 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":9} -->\\\\nP2: When `executeUnshare` rejects before invalidating the directory, this branch still drains the prequeued task and removes the grant from the directory. Reconcile only after unshare invalidation has actually occurred, and leave validation failures without directory changes.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts, line 1291:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>When `executeUnshare` rejects before invalidating the directory, this branch still drains the prequeued task and removes the grant from the directory. Reconcile only after unshare invalidation has actually occurred, and leave validation failures without directory changes.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -1116,24 +1253,45 @@ export async function executePush(\\\\n+            }\\\\n+          }\\\\n+        } else {\\\\n+          await reconcilePermissionDirectoryAfterSettlement(\\\\n+            mut.operation === \\\\\\\"unshare\\\\\\\",\\\\n+          );\\\\n</file context>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\",\\n        \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825497610\\\",\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-20T21:29:12Z\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0R\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"datafn/server/src/execution/transact.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 87,\\n      \\\"comment\\\": {\\n        \\\"author\\\": {\\n          \\\"login\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=3c7263bc-9ecb-4085-ad47-7bd1e801ad74 -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=3775059c-56d5-4810-9e66-69dd9a699541 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":8} -->\\\\nP2: When an `unshare` is invalid, unauthorized, or deduplicated, this loop still creates a durable reconciliation task before the mutation runs. The task can be retried indefinitely when its payload cannot be reconciled, so create it only after validation succeeds or discard it whenever the mutation exits before execution.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/server/src/execution/transact.ts, line 87:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>When an `unshare` is invalid, unauthorized, or deduplicated, this loop still creates a durable reconciliation task before the mutation runs. The task can be retried indefinitely when its payload cannot be reconciled, so create it only after validation succeeds or discard it whenever the mutation exits before execution.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -53,15 +60,115 @@ export async function executeTransaction(\\\\n+        // Atomic unshare removes the external grant before its transaction\\\\n+        // settles. Queue repair on the outer adapter before entering the\\\\n+        // transaction so enqueue failure aborts before invalidation.\\\\n+        const taskId = await enqueuePermissionDirectorySync(\\\\n+          db,\\\\n+          step.mutation,\\\\n</file context>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\",\\n        \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825497611\\\",\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-20T21:29:12Z\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0U\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": null,\\n      \\\"comment\\\": {\\n        \\\"author\\\": {\\n          \\\"login\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=356ba6d5-0686-4d5d-9601-ce0713190d84 -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=3775059c-56d5-4810-9e66-69dd9a699541 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":8} -->\\\\nP2: When an explicit drain races with the interval drainer, this delete can remove the other drainer's claimed task because `taskWhere` contains only `id`. Carry the observed or claimed `next_attempt_at` into the delete and retry update to preserve ownership fencing.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/permission-directory-outbox.ts, line 339:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>When an explicit drain races with the interval drainer, this delete can remove the other drainer's claimed task because `taskWhere` contains only `id`. Carry the observed or claimed `next_attempt_at` into the delete and retry update to preserve ownership fencing.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -0,0 +1,402 @@\\\\n+      String(task.namespace),\\\\n+      runtime,\\\\n+    );\\\\n+    const deleted = await db.internal.delete(OUTBOX