{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:39:13.408Z","ordinal":23734,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_077ca705e7ea3749016a8773f28ea881919e9a0c3f2cc016d8","status":"completed","call_id":"call_8So1xCb5nHv8gU5Xm3YP2M0v","name":"exec","input":"const repoWd=\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/review-followup-next-2026-08-20\";\nconst items=[\n  [\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0D\",\"Fixed in ffa358eb. New public-link credentials are now persisted revoked and are activated only after the share succeeds, so even a failed rollback delete leaves a non-authorizing credential. Added a regression covering share failure plus cleanup failure. DataFn Server: 969 passed, 1 skipped; typecheck and build pass.\"],\n  [\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0J\",\"Fixed in ffa358eb. Raw fallback grants now normalize resource_region into resourceRegion before regional filtering. Added a regression proving a snake-case grant from another region is rejected. DataFn Server: 969 passed, 1 skipped; typecheck and build pass.\"],\n  [\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0N\",\"Fixed in ffa358eb. The many-one validation index now uses the target resource when both relation and FK aliases are omitted, matching runtime derivation. Added a regression that derives projectsId and rejects undefinedId. DataFn Server: 969 passed, 1 skipped; typecheck and build pass.\"],\n  [\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0Q\",\"Investigated in ffa358eb; no production behavior change is needed here. Settlement calls syncDatafnPermissionGrantAfterCommit, which recomputes the deterministic grant id, reads the authoritative database row, and re-indexes an existing grant; an invalid principal is a no-op. Added a regression proving a rejected creator unshare preserves the directory grant and drains the task. DataFn Server: 969 passed, 1 skipped; typecheck and build pass.\"],\n  [\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0R\",\"Investigated in ffa358eb; the prequeue is required before fail-closed external invalidation. Every atomic and sequential exit path drains the prequeued tasks, and the drain reconciles from authoritative database state before deleting the task. Added a regression proving a rejected creator unshare preserves the grant and leaves zero queued tasks. DataFn Server: 969 passed, 1 skipped; typecheck and build pass.\"],\n  [\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0U\",\"Fixed in ffa358eb. Explicit settlement now fences both delete and retry update with the next_attempt_at value observed during lookup, so a later interval claim cannot be erased. Added an interleaving regression that proves the newly claimed task survives. DataFn Server: 969 passed, 1 skipped; typecheck and build pass.\"],\n  [\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0V\",\"Fixed in ffa358eb. Regenerated the checked-in PlugFn example schema; it now includes claim_token and the unique idx_plugfn_sync_jobs_claim_token index. The example TypeScript compile passes, and PlugFn has 236 passing tests plus passing typecheck/build.\"],\n  [\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0X\",\"Investigated and corrected the actual versioning issue in ffa358eb. The base already had schema version 6 and job-scoped claim tokens; all valid v6 application-generated tokens embed the unique job id, so valid v6 rows cannot contain the proposed duplicates. The new length/unique constraint is now correctly introduced as schema version 7, with the generated example updated. An arbitrary destructive dedup migration was therefore not added. PlugFn: 236 tests, typecheck, build, and example compile all pass.\"],\n  [\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a9x0a\",\"Fixed in ffa358eb. Push sanitization now uses a truthiness fallback from fkField to the legacy foreignKey alias. Added a regression proving an empty preferred alias preserves legacyParentId. DataFn Client: 645 tests, typecheck, and build all pass.\"]\n];\nconst q=s=>\"'\"+s.replace(/'/g,\"'\\\"'\\\"'\")+\"'\";\nfor (const [id,body] of items) {\n  const replyQuery=\"mutation($threadId:ID!,$body:String!){addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(input:{pullRequestReviewThreadId:$threadId,body:$body}){comment{id url}}}\";\n  const replyCmd=`GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql -f query=${q(replyQuery)} -F threadId=${q(id)} -f body=${q(body)} --jq '.data.addPullRequestReviewThreadReply.comment | [.id,.url] | @tsv'`;\n  const reply=await tools.exec_command({cmd:replyCmd,workdir:repoWd,yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:1000});\n  if (reply.exit_code!==0) { text(`reply failed ${id}: ${reply.output}`); exit(); }\n  const resolveQuery=\"mutation($threadId:ID!){resolveReviewThread(input:{threadId:$threadId}){thread{id isResolved}}}\";\n  const resolveCmd=`GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql -f query=${q(resolveQuery)} -F threadId=${q(id)} --jq '.data.resolveReviewThread.thread | [.id,.isResolved] | @tsv'`;\n  const resolved=await tools.exec_command({cmd:resolveCmd,workdir:repoWd,yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:1000});\n  if (resolved.exit_code!==0) { text(`resolve failed ${id}: ${resolved.output}`); exit(); }\n  text(`${id} reply=${reply.output.trim()} resolve=${resolved.output.trim()}`);\n}\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787261929.873995}}}
