{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:49:37.172Z","ordinal":23855,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_077ca705e7ea3749016a87766e7b7c8191901380c77b36dfe8","status":"completed","call_id":"call_c4ZGweopuvBBHIAQtiDAo7wb","name":"exec","input":"const cmd=`GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql --paginate \\\n-F owner=21nCo -F name=super-functions.next -F number=46 \\\n-f query='query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!,$endCursor:String){repository(owner:$owner,name:$name){pullRequest(number:$number){headRefOid reviewThreads(first:100,after:$endCursor){nodes{id isResolved path line comments(first:30){nodes{author{login} body url createdAt}}}pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}}}' \\\n| jq -s '{head: .[0].data.repository.pullRequest.headRefOid, total: ([.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]] | length), unresolved: [.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved == false) | {id,path,line,comments: .comments.nodes}]}'`;\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd,workdir:\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/review-followup-next-2026-08-20\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:10000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787262572.638212}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:49:37.875Z","ordinal":23856,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a02126-acd3-7f81-a77d-d46fd838c821","call_id":"call_c4ZGweopuvBBHIAQtiDAo7wb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"949b25\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.518746209,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":598,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"ffa358eb0b2198cbad658bafee8822b849a4c4ae\\\",\\n  \\\"total\\\": 12,\\n  \\\"unresolved\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a-CRg\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"datafn/client/src/sync/engine.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1610,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": {\\n            \\\"login\\\": \\\"chatgpt-codex-connector\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve post-delete writes during compacted replay**\\\\n\\\\nWhen a missing record has a sequence such as `merge(m1)`, `delete(m2)`, then `insert(m3)`, compaction initially sends `m2,m3`; if the delete fails with `NOT_FOUND` while `m3` succeeds, this filter replays `m1,m2,m3`. The server deduplicates the already-applied `m3`, so the replayed delete becomes the final operation, permanently deleting the record even though the client intended to recreate it; the combined results then acknowledge the whole changelog. The replay must preserve later writes that already applied, rather than replaying the failed prefix ahead of their deduplicated IDs.\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825598602\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-20T21:44:58Z\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a-CRm\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"datafn/server/src/plugins/public-links.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 800,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": {\\n            \\\"login\\\": \\\"chatgpt-codex-connector\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Clean up a grant when public-link activation fails**\\\\n\\\\nIf this database update fails after `executeShare` has succeeded, the error is outside the preceding cleanup block: the request returns an error without the token, but the permission grant and revoked public-link row remain. With a permission-directory runtime, the prequeued task's heartbeat is also never stopped, so the background drainer cannot reconcile it while this process remains alive. Activation needs failure handling that compensates the successful share and settles the pending directory task.\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825598610\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-20T21:44:58Z\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787262577.875163}}}
