{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T22:01:11.052Z","ordinal":24043,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_077ca705e7ea3749016a87792406648191a150ee13cdb9ea7e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_XF5gYkwNsEQ5CUBdHPEvH6RC","name":"exec","input":"const cmd=`GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql --paginate -F owner=21nCo -F name=super-functions.next -F number=46 -f query='query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!,$endCursor:String){repository(owner:$owner,name:$name){pullRequest(number:$number){headRefOid reviewThreads(first:100,after:$endCursor){nodes{id isResolved path line comments(first:20){nodes{author{login} body url createdAt}}}pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}}}' | jq -s '{head:.[0].data.repository.pullRequest.headRefOid,total:([.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]]|length),unresolved:[.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]|select(.isResolved==false)|{id,path,line,last:.comments.nodes[-1]}]}'`;\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd,workdir:\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/review-followup-next-2026-08-20\",yield_time_ms:30000,max_output_tokens:6000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787263267.047104}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T22:01:11.987Z","ordinal":24044,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a02131-4433-7ac2-b5d3-0acf2e4e6627","call_id":"call_XF5gYkwNsEQ5CUBdHPEvH6RC","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"6a2f75\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.74844625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":573,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"8f31d783634d0f6f5b6ece414a9c72ec37ab2b6e\\\",\\n  \\\"total\\\": 14,\\n  \\\"unresolved\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a-RG_\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"plugfn/core/src/schema.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 226,\\n      \\\"last\\\": {\\n        \\\"author\\\": {\\n          \\\"login\\\": \\\"chatgpt-codex-connector\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"body\\\": \\\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Allow legacy claim tokens through the v7 migration**\\\\n\\\\nWhen upgrading a MySQL installation from v6, this `maxLength` change converts the existing `TEXT` column to `VARCHAR(64)`. The v6 queue claimer stored `${workerId}:${job.id}:${timestamp}`; even the default generated worker and job IDs produce roughly 66 characters, and caller-provided worker IDs can make it longer. Consequently, an active or stale claimed job can make the generated `ALTER TABLE ... MODIFY COLUMN` fail with “Data too long” (or truncate under permissive SQL modes), blocking or corrupting the v7 migration. Retain a width that accommodates legacy tokens or explicitly transform/clear them before narrowing the column.\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\",\\n        \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825689787\\\",\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-20T21:59:55Z\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a-RHG\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"plugfn/core/src/schema.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 11,\\n      \\\"last\\\": {\\n        \\\"author\\\": {\\n          \\\"login\\\": \\\"chatgpt-codex-connector\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"body\\\": \\\"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Update the published schema-version metadata**\\\\n\\\\nBumping `PLUGFN_SCHEMA_VERSION` to 7 leaves `plugfn/core/package.json` at `superfunctions.schemaVersion: 6`. `discoverSuperfunctionsPackages()` reads and exposes that package metadata, so installed PlugFn packages are still reported as requiring schema version 6 even though `getSchema()` now returns version 7; consumers using discovery metadata to determine required migrations will miss this schema upgrade. Update the package metadata alongside this constant.\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\",\\n        \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825689795\\\",\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-20T21:59:56Z\\\"\\n      }\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787263271.987255}}}
