{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T22:50:17.225Z","ordinal":24763,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_077ca705e7ea3749016a8784a638f4819198fd15b0cba03753","status":"completed","call_id":"call_jrKczFYAFB05iMfY1uyFJ057","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql --paginate -F owner=21nCo -F name=super-functions.next -F number=46 -f query='query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!,$endCursor:String){repository(owner:$owner,name:$name){pullRequest(number:$number){headRefOid reviewThreads(first:100,after:$endCursor){nodes{id isResolved path line comments(first:20){nodes{author{login} body url createdAt}}}pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}}}' | jq -s '{head: .[0].data.repository.pullRequest.headRefOid, total: ([.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]] | length), unresolved: [.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved == false) | {id,path,line,comments}]}'\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/review-followup-next-2026-08-20\",\n  yield_time_ms: 30000,\n  max_output_tokens: 18000\n});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787266212.292781}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T22:50:17.922Z","ordinal":24764,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0215e-37c2-7910-948b-2f108471a4c8","call_id":"call_jrKczFYAFB05iMfY1uyFJ057","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\n  \"head\": \"a06a431ba590b40d328253c76cf9ed0a4d8e139b\",\n  \"total\": 19,\n  \"unresolved\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a-3-5\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/client/src/query.ts\",\n      \"line\": 311,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep displaced remote rows reachable across pagination**\\n\\nWhen a first-page query has a `limit`, allowing the local overlay here can silently skip a remote row during traversal. For example, if the server returns `r1,r2` plus a cursor positioned after `r2`, and a pending local row sorts before them, `mergeQueryDataById` returns `local,r1` after re-limiting but preserves the server cursor; the next page starts after `r2` and bypasses overlays, so `r2` is never delivered. Offset pagination has the same problem because the displaced row remains inside the skipped first server page. Either retain displaced remote rows or avoid overlaying queries whose pagination state cannot be recomputed.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825929533\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T22:47:12Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOQ4ERBM6a-3-_\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/core/src/schema.ts\",\n      \"line\": 304,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Enforce the new ID-prefix invariant in Python**\\n\\nShared schemas validated through `datafn/python/datafn/validation.py::validate_schema` still accept duplicate normalized prefixes such as `project` and `project:` (and also empty prefixes), while this new TypeScript path rejects them. The same schema can therefore start successfully under Python but fail under TypeScript, leaving invalid prefix configurations dependent on which SDK loads them; mirror the normalization and collision checks in Python.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L422-L422](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/blob/a06a431ba590b40d328253c76cf9ed0a4d8e139b/AGENTS.md#L422-L422)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/46#discussion_r3825929539\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-20T22:47:12Z\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","create_time":1787266217.922453}}}
