{"timestamp":"2026-08-20T23:04:47.224Z","ordinal":24967,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a01efc-6d32-70b2-a5a3-6d2475cf5417","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"item-1395","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"A new late thread arrived during the final guard, so the merge correctly remains blocked. It identifies one more TypeScript/Python schema-parity gap: Python accepts a non-string legacy `foreignKey` alias that TypeScript now rejects. I’m applying that narrow validator parity fix with a regression, then I’ll rerun the Python suite and restart the exact-head review cycle."}],"phase":"commentary"},"completed_at_ms":1787267087224}}
