{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T04:36:04.052Z","ordinal":25149,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0229a-c754-7333-9db1-bace50f94565","call_id":"call_vppWpqcVI4Mm7qPtZ4iB8snG","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"  1348\t\n  1349\t## Task 1: Inventory worktrees and local changes, partial\n  1350\t\n  1351\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1352\t\n  1353\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-10T13-35-02-Oqwo-superfunctions_worktree_inventory.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/10/rollout-2026-08-10T19-05-02-019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T21:42:42+00:00, thread_id=019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0, inventory succeeded but later scope overreach prevented final handoff)\n  1354\t\n  1355\t### keywords\n  1356\t\n  1357\t- `git worktree list --porcelain`, `git status --short --branch`, `git diff --shortstat`, `git rev-list --left-right --count`, `SF-15`, `SFN-15`, `codex/mcpfn`, dirty-worktree, prunable\n  1358\t\n  1359\t## User preferences\n  1360\t\n  1361\t- when the user asks for a worktree summary and the task is framed “strictly read-only” -> inspect only, then return the requested table; do not fetch, merge, push, snapshot, or alter PR state. [Task 1]\n  1362\t\n  1363\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1364\t\n  1365\t- `git worktree list --porcelain` is the authoritative registered-worktree inventory. For each worktree, use `git status --short --branch`, `git diff --shortstat`, `git diff --name-status`, `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`, and `git rev-list --left-right --count \"$branch...$remote\"`; separate tracked source, untracked artifacts, and disk consumption. [Task 1]\n  1366\t- At the inspected snapshot, nine entries included eight live worktrees and one stale/prunable `/private/tmp/sf-docsfn-core-pack-a2712232`. `superfunctions-dev` was a broad dirty integration stack (377 tracked + 95 untracked paths, 10 commits behind stored `origin/dev`); `SFN-15` held large generated `.conduct` evidence; `codex/mcpfn` had 103 modified + 80 untracked paths. Counts and divergence are snapshot-specific. [Task 1]\n  1367\t\n  1368\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1369\t\n  1370\t- Symptom: a divergence loop reports `fatal: ambiguous argument`. Cause: branch and remote were passed as one malformed revision expression. Fix: use separate shell variables and `git rev-list --left-right --count \"$branch...$remote\"`. [Task 1]\n  1371\t- Symptom: a read-only inventory grows into remote reconciliation, merges, or snapshots. Cause: the agent continued after it had enough inspection evidence. Fix: stop after collecting state and return the summary; state explicitly that no files, refs, index entries, or remotes were changed. [Task 1]\n  1372\t\n  1373\t# Task Group: Router Humane analysis audit and evidence-gap hardening in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/router\n  1374\tscope: Use for read-only assessment or evidence-grounded publication of Router's Humane by Design analysis. Keep public-surface observations distinct from authenticated, lifecycle, accessibility, abuse, privacy, and exit behavior.\n  1375\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/router; reuse_rule=reinspect the current module, generated artifacts, and first-party principles before acting; corpus counts and publication state are time-specific.\n  1376\t\n  1377\t## Task 1: Audit Humane analysis and harden the evidence workflow, partial then success\n  1378\t\n  1379\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1380\t\n  1381\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-09T06-23-20-spXF-humane_analysis_read_only_audit_and_authenticated_publicatio.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/router, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/09/rollout-2026-08-09T11-53-20-019fe530-ad6b-78f0-b60c-f4e32ff6ac57.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-13T04:39:05+00:00, thread_id=019fe530-ad6b-78f0-b60c-f4e32ff6ac57, heuristic Humane audit plus gated authenticated publication verification)\n  1382\t\n  1383\t### keywords\n  1384\t\n  1385\t- Humane by Design, humanebydesign.v1, analysis.humane@1, heuristic scoring, evidence v2, Partial / Suppressed, unknown, critical evidence, acquisition manifest, Humanefactor\n  3067\t# Task Group: superfunctions-dev dirty-worktree provenance in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\n  3068\tscope: Use for read-only inventories of the linked Superfunctions dev checkout and provenance tracing through Nucleus and sibling `.conduct` records.\n  3069\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree size/origin evidence is snapshot-specific; re-run Git and consumer-log checks before attributing new changes.\n  3070\t\n  3071\t## Task 1: Inventory dirty changes and trace their origin, success\n  3072\t\n  3073\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3074\t\n  3075\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/04/rollout-2026-08-04T17-11-28-019fcc94-2243-7543-81c9-399c9871de91.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T11:50:19+00:00, thread_id=019fcc94-2243-7543-81c9-399c9871de91, read-only 470-path inventory with direct-versus-inferred provenance)\n  3076\t\n  3077\t### keywords\n  3078\t\n  3079\t- superfunctions-dev, Nucleus, AuthFn, DataFn, SearchFn, FileFn, file: dependencies, symlinked-local-packages, root-source-fix, .conduct, 377 files changed\n  3080\t\n  3081\t## User preferences\n  3082\t\n  3083\t- when the user says “all read-only” -> do not edit, stage, commit, fetch, or create artifacts. [Task 1]\n  3084\t- when asking to inspect other projects’ `.conduct` folders and local DataFn/AuthFn usage -> cite exact manifests/logs and separate direct evidence, strong inference, and unresolved provenance. [Task 1]\n  3085\t\n  3086\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3087\t\n  3088\t- This was a large uncommitted integration stack: `377` tracked files changed (`+20,131/-9,758`), 15 deletions, 93 untracked paths, 470 affected paths overall; DataFn and AuthFn were the largest areas. [Task 1]\n  3089\t- Nucleus consumes this checkout through `file:` dependencies and its `.conduct` records specific root-source fixes for DataFn IndexedDB/clone/filter/sort/relation behavior, SearchFn exact matching, and DataFn push retryability/stale mutation recovery. Local linked source may diverge from registry-pinned CI/production packages. [Task 1]\n  3090\t- Exponential e0, Pagerrr, and Skillplane evidence did not directly attribute the stack to those projects; broad AuthFn modularization is strongly inferred from Nucleus, while SearchFn/FileFn/observability provenance remains unresolved. [Task 1]\n  3091\t\n  3092\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3093\t\n  3094\t- Symptom: provenance report asserts every dirty file came from one consumer. Cause: mixed direct evidence and inference. Fix: identify evidence level per area; do not treat a stale local `origin/dev` view as freshly fetched state. [Task 1]\n  3095\t- Symptom: deleted paths break timestamp inspection or an exploratory `awk` comparison errors. Fix: use Git metadata for deleted files and exclude failed command branches from provenance evidence. [Task 1]\nREDACTED.md\nREDACTED.md\nREDACTED.md\n2026-08-10T13-35-02-Oqwo-superfunctions_worktree_inventory.md\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0229a-8394-7dc3-88d3-07bbf870a918","create_time":1787286964.052149}}}
