{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T04:49:10.843Z","ordinal":25387,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a0229a-8394-7dc3-88d3-07bbf870a918","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"item-1443","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Next phase is complete. No PR was merged.\n\n- Created [PR #47](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/47) against `sf-next/next`.\n  - Commit: `ba898b4739f255cbc4c5866af17b2833cce6fc23`\n  - Deletes four tracked WatchFn `.next` build artifacts (~5.5 MB).\n  - Review threads: **0 total, 0 unresolved**.\n  - PR remains open and unmerged.\n\n- No `origin/dev` PR was created. Replaying the preserved dev snapshot showed that valid functional work was already integrated. The remaining differences were stale or broken, including dependency cycles, duplicated implementations, and invalid test syntax.\n\n- CI attribution:\n  - CodeRabbit, Cubic, Graphite, GitGuardian, Socket, and planning passed.\n  - JavaScript failed on the pre-existing ProbeFn Turbo dependency cycle.\n  - Guardrails failed on pre-existing LangFn duplication.\n  - Pullfrog failed with a missing authentication header.\n  - Three Vercel jobs failed because private-organization repositories cannot deploy on the Hobby plan.\n\n- `.conduct` was unchanged.\n- `.gitignore` was unchanged because `.next/` is already ignored.\n- Both original dirty worktrees remain untouched at their original HEADs and exact dirty-file counts.\n\nThe remaining decision is whether to repair or waive the unrelated baseline CI failures before merging PR #47.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":3067,"lineEnd":3094,"note":"used prior dirty dev provenance and snapshot cautions while reconciling the preserved local stack"},{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":1349,"lineEnd":1371,"note":"used prior worktree inventory guidance to verify registered worktrees and current dirty state"}],"rolloutI