{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:01:02.789Z","ordinal":25414,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a022b1-a5c5-7a10-904c-c0bc3c164194","call_id":"call_85L6oNg4PBODX8QDOpbpxq2s","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"fc622d\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3100,\"output\":\"applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/{superfunctions,superfunctions-dev,worktrees/superfunctions/*}; reuse_rule=verify current ref, account, and package state; counts/SHA/release status are time-specific.\\n\\n## Task 1: Audit PR #34 and ecosystem production readiness, partial/NO-GO\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/11/rollout-2026-08-11T18-00-16-019ff0cd-53a5-7f52-aa68-e992f6213ecc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-11T12:35:05+00:00, thread_id=019ff0cd-53a5-7f52-aa68-e992f6213ecc, environment scope bypass reproduced)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- PR #34, secfn, environmentId, resolveScope, SFN-18, 721eefdd, ProbeFn Turbo cycle, NO-GO\\n\\n## Task 2: Publish next-only npm packages and remediate McpFn PR #42, success\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/11/rollout-2026-08-11T18-23-27-019ff0e2-8dd1-7782-ac67-85708209c32d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-12T14:04:47+00:00, thread_id=019ff0e2-8dd1-7782-ac67-85708209c32d, 47/47 exact npm versions verified; reusable hosted Skillplane release skill published)\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mcpfn, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/11/rollout-2026-08-11T19-22-58-019ff119-0aba-71c3-8cdd-4f55708790de.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-12T10:40:33+00:00, thread_id=019ff119-0aba-71c3-8cdd-4f55708790de, five intended fixes and the Rollup CI repair pushed; PR #42 merged into sf-next/next)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- sf-next/next, origin/dev, publish-tag.yml, @plugfn/providers, package isolation, PR #42, gate:mcpfn-release, Node 24, MemoryFn, @rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu, --match-head-commit\\n\\n## Task 3: Compare local next and dev worktree state, success\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- sf-next/next, origin/dev, 93 ahead, dev..next, common-scope comparison, dirty worktree\\n\\n## Task 4: Remediate current PR #103 review findings locally, success\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SF-8-ci-fixes, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/11/rollout-2026-08-11T18-06-59-019ff0d3-7b1f-7e03-ab55-c5c5fd150841.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T12:58:28+00:00, thread_id=019ff0d3-7b1f-7e03-ab55-c5c5fd150841, reviewed fixes pushed and PR #103 merged with exact-head guard)\\n\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- PR #103, SF-8, `21n/report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0`, `reviewThreads`, GraphQL, Outlook SSRF, checkpoint null, Python rate limit, `0cea01c4`, `git push origin HEAD:SF-8`\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- preserve a dirty checkout and use an isolated exact-head worktree for audit/release work; “what do you think?” and “resume” requested review, not remediation. [Task 1]\\n- publish only packages changed since latest npm release, excluding dev-present/shared packages unless explicitly included. [Task 2]\\n- when the user asked for “splane PR fixes” -> retrieve the live hosted workflow, write/reconcile evidence before edits, and preserve an existing dirty PR checkout by using a dedicated exact-head worktree. Push only after explicit authorization and an exact-head remote guard. [Task 4]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- `sf-next/next`, not `origin/next`, is the valid next ref. In private 21n repos, use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` if default `gh` returns misleading 404. Test caller-supplied `environmentId` where IDs outrank environment scope. [Task 1]\\n- Package releases require package-local install/build/test/pack and dependency-safe batches. Failed immutable `@plugfn/providers@0.0.1` required corrected `0.0.2`; do not reuse failed tags. [Task 2]\\n- McpFn release gate needs Node 24; a root install can mask standalone dependencies. In hosted McpFn CI, run `node scripts/ci-install-rollup-native.mjs` after `npm ci` before the gate because npm can omit `@rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu`. Validate post-push local/ref/PR SHA equality and merge with an exact-head guard. [Task 2]\\n- Worktree snapshots are cache-relative without fetch; take final counts after detailed inspection if a checkout changes concurrently. [Task 3]\\n- For private Superfunctions PRs, inspect authenticated current `reviewThreads`/head comments, including `isResolved` and `isOutdated`, before editing. PR #103 used a clean isolated exact-head worktree because the existing checkout was dirty; after user authorization, fetch `origin/SF-8`, require it to equal `HEAD^`, then push `HEAD:SF-8` and verify local/remote/live PR SHA equality. [Task 4]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- Passing focused PR tests missed `resolveScope()` precedence; external billing/CI gaps are separate from code correctness. [Task 1]\\n- Do not dispatch all tag releases sharing one concurrency group. Remove sibling-source aliases and root-tool assumptions from package tests; do not attribute generic JavaScript, Python, Vercel, or dependency-cycle baseline failures to McpFn without the exact job logs. [Task 2]\\n- A malformed GraphQL query can fail; use paginated `reviewThreads(first:100, after:$cursor)` and check `pageInfo.hasNextPage`. If `python` is absent from PATH, use the bundled runtime via a temporary `python` symlink before running `node scripts/ci-run-python-package.mjs plugfn/python`; keep full-repository baseline failures separate from changed-surface tests. [Task 4]\\n- Omitting the explicit Worker route can make `/` redirect while deep paths serve stale content. Purge cache after adding the route. [Task 1]\\n- Existing Svelte/Vite/Vitest startup failed with `TypeError: Cannot convert undefined or null to object`; use Node built-in tests for the focused redirect worker and do not treat that baseline as redirect failure. [Task 1]\\n\\n# Task Group: Superfunctions worktree inventory in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions\\nscope: Use for a read-only inventory of registered Superfunctions worktrees and local-change magnitude. Separate tracked source, untracked artifacts, disk consumption, and cache-relative remote divergence.\\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions; reuse_rule=inventory counts and branch/upstream state are snapshots; rerun the listed commands and do not mutate unless authorized.\\n\\n## Task 1: Inventory worktrees and local changes, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-10T13-35-02-Oqwo-superfunctions_worktree_inventory.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/10/rollout-2026-08-10T19-05-02-019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T21:42:42+00:00, thread_id=019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0, inventory succeeded but later scope overreach prevented final handoff)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- `git worktree list --porcelain`, `git status --short --branch`, `git diff --shortstat`, `git rev-list --left-right --count`, `SF-15`, `SFN-15`, `codex/mcpfn`, dirty-worktree, prunable\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when the user asks for a worktree summary and the task is framed “strictly read-only” -> inspect only, then return the requested table; do not fetch, merge, push, snapshot, or alter PR state. [Task 1]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- `git worktree list --porcelain` is the authoritative registered-worktree inventory. For each worktree, use `git status --short --branch`, `git diff --shortstat`, `git diff --name-status`, `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`, and `git rev-list --left-right --count \\\"$branch...$remote\\\"`; separate tracked source, untracked artifacts, and disk consumption. [Task 1]\\n- At the inspected snapshot, nine entries included eight live worktrees and one stale/prunable `/private/tmp/sf-docsfn-core-pack-a2712232`. `superfunctions-dev` was a broad dirty integration stack (377 tracked + 95 untracked paths, 10 commits behind stored `origin/dev`); `SFN-15` held large generated `.conduct` evidence; `codex/mcpfn` had 103 modified + 80 untracked paths. Counts and divergence are snapshot-specific. [Task 1]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- Symptom: a divergence loop reports `fatal: ambiguous argument`. Cause: branch and remote were passed as one malformed revision expression. Fix: use separate shell variables and `git rev-list --left-right --count \\\"$branch...$remote\\\"`. [Task 1]\\n- Symptom: a read-only inventory grows into remote reconciliation, merges, or snapshots. Cause: the agent continued after it had enough inspection evidence. Fix: stop after collecting state and return the summary; state explicitly that no files, refs, index entries, or remotes were changed. [Task 1]\\n\\n# Task Group: Router Humane analysis audit and evidence-gap hardening in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/router\\nscope: Use for read-only assessment or evidence-grounded publication of Router's Humane by Design analysis. Keep public-surface observations distinct from authenticated, lifecycle, accessibility, abuse, privacy, and exit behavior.\\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/router; reuse_rule=reinspect the current module, generated artifacts, and first-party principles before acting; corpus counts and publication state are time-specific.\\n\\n## Task 1: Audit Humane analysis and harden the evidence workflow, partial then success\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n# Task Group: superfunctions-dev dirty-worktree provenance in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\\nscope: Use for read-only inventories of the linked Superfunctions dev checkout and provenance tracing through Nucleus and sibling `.conduct` records.\\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree size/origin evidence is snapshot-specific; re-run Git and consumer-log checks before attributing new changes.\\n\\n## Task 1: Inventory dirty changes and trace their origin, success\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/04/rollout-2026-08-04T17-11-28-019fcc94-2243-7543-81c9-399c9871de91.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T11:50:19+00:00, thread_id=019fcc94-2243-7543-81c9-399c9871de91, read-only 470-path inventory with direct-versus-inferred provenance)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- superfunctions-dev, Nucleus, AuthFn, DataFn, SearchFn, FileFn, file: dependencies, symlinked-local-packages, root-source-fix, .conduct, 377 files changed\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when the user says “all read-only” -> do not edit, stage, commit, fetch, or create artifacts. [Task 1]\\n- when asking to inspect other projects’ `.conduct` folders and local DataFn/AuthFn usage -> cite exact manifests/logs and separate direct evidence, strong inference, and unresolved provenance. [Task 1]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- This was a large uncommitted integration stack: `377` tracked files changed (`+20,131/-9,758`), 15 deletions, 93 untracked paths, 470 affected paths overall; DataFn and AuthFn were the largest areas. [Task 1]\\n- Nucleus consumes this checkout through `file:` dependencies and its `.conduct` records specific root-source fixes for DataFn IndexedDB/clone/filter/sort/relation behavior, SearchFn exact matching, and DataFn push retryability/stale mutation recovery. Local linked source may diverge from registry-pinned CI/production packages. [Task 1]\\n- Exponential e0, Pagerrr, and Skillplane evidence did not directly attribute the stack to those projects; broad AuthFn modularization is strongly inferred from Nucleus, while SearchFn/FileFn/observability provenance remains unresolved. [Task 1]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- Symptom: provenance report asserts every dirty file came from one consumer. Cause: mixed direct evidence and inference. Fix: identify evidence level per area; do not treat a stale local `origin/dev` view as freshly fetched state. [Task 1]\\n- Symptom: deleted paths break timestamp inspection or an exploratory `awk` comparison errors. Fix: use Git metadata for deleted files and exclude failed command branches from provenance evidence. [Task 1]\\n\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a022b1-36ac-7732-bf2d-a946dee5da2c","create_time":1787288462.789872}}}
