{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:02:56.428Z","ordinal":25455,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a022b3-61ac-72c0-b588-763c428aaed4","call_id":"call_fYe1qVhGliO8KG3JEFVcNZ4f","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e3c866\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002417,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1763,\"output\":\"  1065\\t- PR #103, SF-8, `21n/report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0`, `reviewThreads`, GraphQL, Outlook SSRF, checkpoint null, Python rate limit, `0cea01c4`, `git push origin HEAD:SF-8`\\n  1066\\t\\n  1067\\t## User preferences\\n  1068\\t\\n  1069\\t- preserve a dirty checkout and use an isolated exact-head worktree for audit/release work; “what do you think?” and “resume” requested review, not remediation. [Task 1]\\n  1070\\t- publish only packages changed since latest npm release, excluding dev-present/shared packages unless explicitly included. [Task 2]\\n  1071\\t- when the user asked for “splane PR fixes” -> retrieve the live hosted workflow, write/reconcile evidence before edits, and preserve an existing dirty PR checkout by using a dedicated exact-head worktree. Push only after explicit authorization and an exact-head remote guard. [Task 4]\\n  1072\\t\\n  1073\\t## Reusable knowledge\\n  1074\\t\\n  1075\\t- `sf-next/next`, not `origin/next`, is the valid next ref. In private 21n repos, use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` if default `gh` returns misleading 404. Test caller-supplied `environmentId` where IDs outrank environment scope. [Task 1]\\n  1076\\t- Package releases require package-local install/build/test/pack and dependency-safe batches. Failed immutable `@plugfn/providers@0.0.1` required corrected `0.0.2`; do not reuse failed tags. [Task 2]\\n  1077\\t- McpFn release gate needs Node 24; a root install can mask standalone dependencies. In hosted McpFn CI, run `node scripts/ci-install-rollup-native.mjs` after `npm ci` before the gate because npm can omit `@rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu`. Validate post-push local/ref/PR SHA equality and merge with an exact-head guard. [Task 2]\\n  1078\\t- Worktree snapshots are cache-relative without fetch; take final counts after detailed inspection if a checkout changes concurrently. [Task 3]\\n  1079\\t- For private Superfunctions PRs, inspect authenticated current `reviewThreads`/head comments, including `isResolved` and `isOutdated`, before editing. PR #103 used a clean isolated exact-head worktree because the existing checkout was dirty; after user authorization, fetch `origin/SF-8`, require it to equal `HEAD^`, then push `HEAD:SF-8` and verify local/remote/live PR SHA equality. [Task 4]\\n  1080\\t\\n  1081\\t## Failures and how to do differently\\n  1082\\t\\n  1424\\t\\n  1425\\t## User preferences\\n  1426\\t\\n  1427\\t- when the user asks for a worktree summary and the task is framed “strictly read-only” -> inspect only, then return the requested table; do not fetch, merge, push, snapshot, or alter PR state. [Task 1]\\n  1428\\t\\n  1429\\t## Reusable knowledge\\n  1430\\t\\n  1431\\t- `git worktree list --porcelain` is the authoritative registered-worktree inventory. For each worktree, use `git status --short --branch`, `git diff --shortstat`, `git diff --name-status`, `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`, and `git rev-list --left-right --count \\\"$branch...$remote\\\"`; separate tracked source, untracked artifacts, and disk consumption. [Task 1]\\n  1432\\t- At the inspected snapshot, nine entries included eight live worktrees and one stale/prunable `/private/tmp/sf-docsfn-core-pack-a2712232`. `superfunctions-dev` was a broad dirty integration stack (377 tracked + 95 untracked paths, 10 commits behind stored `origin/dev`); `SFN-15` held large generated `.conduct` evidence; `codex/mcpfn` had 103 modified + 80 untracked paths. Counts and divergence are snapshot-specific. [Task 1]\\n  1433\\t\\n  1434\\t## Failures and how to do differently\\n  1435\\t\\n  1436\\t- Symptom: a divergence loop reports `fatal: ambiguous argument`. Cause: branch and remote were passed as one malformed revision expression. Fix: use separate shell variables and `git rev-list --left-right --count \\\"$branch...$remote\\\"`. [Task 1]\\n  1437\\t- Symptom: a read-only inventory grows into remote reconciliation, merges, or snapshots. Cause: the agent continued after it had enough inspection evidence. Fix: stop after collecting state and return the summary; state explicitly that no files, refs, index entries, or remotes were changed. [Task 1]\\n  1438\\t\\n  3133\\t# Task Group: superfunctions-dev dirty-worktree provenance in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\\n  3134\\tscope: Use for read-only inventories of the linked Superfunctions dev checkout and provenance tracing through Nucleus and sibling `.conduct` records.\\n  3135\\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree size/origin evidence is snapshot-specific; re-run Git and consumer-log checks before attributing new changes.\\n  3136\\t\\n  3137\\t## Task 1: Inventory dirty changes and trace their origin, success\\n  3138\\t\\n  3139\\t### rollout_summary_files\\n  3140\\t\\n  3141\\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/04/rollout-2026-08-04T17-11-28-019fcc94-2243-7543-81c9-399c9871de91.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T11:50:19+00:00, thread_id=019fcc94-2243-7543-81c9-399c9871de91, read-only 470-path inventory with direct-versus-inferred provenance)\\n  3142\\t\\n  3143\\t### keywords\\n  3144\\t\\n  3145\\t- superfunctions-dev, Nucleus, AuthFn, DataFn, SearchFn, FileFn, file: dependencies, symlinked-local-packages, root-source-fix, .conduct, 377 files changed\\n  3146\\t\\n  3147\\t## User preferences\\n  3148\\t\\n  3149\\t- when the user says “all read-only” -> do not edit, stage, commit, fetch, or create artifacts. [Task 1]\\n  3150\\t- when asking to inspect other projects’ `.conduct` folders and local DataFn/AuthFn usage -> cite exact manifests/logs and separate direct evidence, strong inference, and unresolved provenance. [Task 1]\\n  3151\\t\\n  3152\\t## Reusable knowledge\\n  3153\\t\\n  3154\\t- This was a large uncommitted integration stack: `377` tracked files changed (`+20,131/-9,758`), 15 deletions, 93 untracked paths, 470 affected paths overall; DataFn and AuthFn were the largest areas. [Task 1]\\n  3155\\t- Nucleus consumes this checkout through `file:` dependencies and its `.conduct` records specific root-source fixes for DataFn IndexedDB/clone/filter/sort/relation behavior, SearchFn exact matching, and DataFn push retryability/stale mutation recovery. Local linked source may diverge from registry-pinned CI/production packages. [Task 1]\\n  3156\\t- Exponential e0, Pagerrr, and Skillplane evidence did not directly attribute the stack to those projects; broad AuthFn modularization is strongly inferred from Nucleus, while SearchFn/FileFn/observability provenance remains unresolved. [Task 1]\\n  3157\\t\\n  3158\\t## Failures and how to do differently\\n  3159\\t\\n  3160\\t- Symptom: provenance report asserts every dirty file came from one consumer. Cause: mixed direct evidence and inference. Fix: identify evidence level per area; do not treat a stale local `origin/dev` view as freshly fetched state. [Task 1]\\n  3161\\t- Symptom: deleted paths break timestamp inspection or an exploratory `awk` comparison errors. Fix: use Git metadata for deleted files and exclude failed command branches from provenance evidence. [Task 1]\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a022b1-36ac-7732-bf2d-a946dee5da2c","create_time":1787288576.428166}}}
