{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:03:38.681Z","ordinal":25475,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a022b1-36ac-7732-bf2d-a946dee5da2c","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"item-1449","summary_text":["**Analyzing remote and local patch differences**","**Planning non-mutating patch integration analysis**","**Analyzing remote and local patch differences**","**Planning non-mutating patch integration analysis**","**Clarifying local changes integration**","**Investigating residual path list**","**Planning three-way merge to identify residual paths**","**Investigating residual path list**","**Planning three-way merge to identify residual paths**","**Summarizing file change overlap statistics**","**Clarifying excluded and deleted files**","**Explaining residual local changes and cleaning temp file**","**Planning final answer with memory citations**","**Summarizing branch integration and snapshot details**","**Planning final answer with memory citations**","**Summarizing branch integration and snapshot details**"],"raw_content":[]},"completed_at_ms":1787288618681}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:03:38.681Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"content":null,"id":"rs_077ca705e7ea3749016a87dc26d6ec8191bdee530fd9cba7d1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a022b1-36ac-7732-bf2d-a946dee5da2c"},"summary":[{"text":"**Planning final answer with memory citations**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Summarizing branch integration and snapshot details**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:03:55.632Z","ordinal":25477,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a022b1-36ac-7732-bf2d-a946dee5da2c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"item-1450","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"You’re right—the earlier wording was too broad. A more accurate statement is: most local work was deliberately transferred through PR #114 and then hardened by PR #115; the remaining local-only remnants were reviewed and excluded. :codex-annotation{index=\"1\"}\n\nWhat happened:\n\n1. The dirty `superfunctions-dev` worktree was based on `713f82b3`.\n2. We preserved all its uncommitted work in snapshot `5e867bf9`: 472 paths, including 362 modifications, 95 additions, and 15 deletions.\n3. We did not commit directly from that dirty worktree. We replayed/reconciled it in the isolated `codex/dev-integration-2026-08-19` worktree.\n4. That integration became [PR #114](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/114), merged into `dev`.\n5. Review remediation then became [PR #115](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115), which was also merged.\n6. The original dirty worktree was intentionally left untouched, so it still displays the original local changes even though their reconciled versions are now in `origin/dev`.\n\nThe live three-way comparison confirms this:\n\n| Classification | Paths |\n|---|---:|\n| Current `origin/dev` is byte-for-byte identical to the local snapshot | 289 |\n| Current `origin/dev` contains a subsequently changed/reviewed version | 183 |\n| Remote still had the old base version—truly untouched local-only paths | 0 |\n\nPR overlap explains where they went:\n\n- PR #114 overlapped **466 of the 472** local snapshot paths.\n- PRs #109, #114, and #115 together overlapped **468 of 472** paths.\n- Those overlap counts are not additive because some files were touched by multiple PRs.\n- The remaining four were:\n  - two `.conduct` artifacts intentionally excluded from a `dev` PR;\n  - two obsolete AuthFn documentation paths that were replaced/deleted remotely.\n\nAlso, the snapshot’s base is now **176 commits behind** current `origin/dev`, not merely a few commits behind. Those intervening commits include:\n\n- [PR #109](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/109): shared-package production work.\n- [PR #114](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/114): explicit integration of the local AuthFn, DataFn, FileFn, SearchFn, storage, observability, and delivery work.\n- [PR #115](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115): extensive review-driven durability, concurrency, migration, and consistency fixes.\n\nWhen the original snapshot was replayed again after those merges, only 18 files produced residual differences. Those were not silently considered integrated; they were explicitly reviewed and rejected because they included:\n\n- AuthFn dependency declarations that recreated a Turbo dependency cycle.\n- Removal of valid AuthFn workspaces.\n- Duplicate documentation blocks.\n- Invalid DataFn test syntax.\n- Duplicate idempotency and reconciliation implementations.\n- Older permission-directory behavior superseded by durable post-commit recovery.\n- An unused CLI import.\n- An older fixed-window rate-limit implementation superseded by the reviewed CAS implementation.\n\nSo the important distinction is:\n\n- **289 files:** literally integrated.\n- **165 of the other 183 files:** effectively absorbed or further evolved during reconciliation/review.\n- **18 files:** remaining local deltas deliberately not carried forward.\n- **Original worktree:** still dirty because preservation—not cleanup—was the policy.\n\nTherefore, no new `dev` PR was created in the last phase because PR #114 had already been the principal PR for those local changes, and PR #115 had already carried their review corrections. It was not because all 472 files independently appeared on remote by coincidence.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":3133,"lineEnd":3160,"note":"used the prior dirty dev provenance inventory to contextualize the local AuthFn and DataFn integration stack"},{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":1429,"lineEnd":1432,"note":"used the prior worktree inventory guidance and preserved dirty-worktree counts"}],"rolloutIds":["019fcc94-2243-7543-81c9-399c9871de91","019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0"]}},"completed_at_ms":1787288635632}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:03:55.644Z","ordinal":25478,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_077ca705e7ea3749016a87dc2a98388191876f95bc7cc35b33","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"You’re right—the earlier wording was too broad. A more accurate statement is: most local work was deliberately transferred through PR #114 and then hardened by PR #115; the remaining local-only remnants were reviewed and excluded. :codex-annotation{index=\"1\"}\n\nWhat happened:\n\n1. The dirty `superfunctions-dev` worktree was based on `713f82b3`.\n2. We preserved all its uncommitted work in snapshot `5e867bf9`: 472 paths, including 362 modifications, 95 additions, and 15 deletions.\n3. We did not commit directly from that dirty worktree. We replayed/reconciled it in the isolated `codex/dev-integration-2026-08-19` worktree.\n4. That integration became [PR #114](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/114), merged into `dev`.\n5. Review remediation then became [PR #115](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115), which was also merged.\n6. The original dirty worktree was intentionally left untouched, so it still displays the original local changes even though their reconciled versions are now in `origin/dev`.\n\nThe live three-way comparison confirms this:\n\n| Classification | Paths |\n|---|---:|\n| Current `origin/dev` is byte-for-byte identical to the local snapshot | 289 |\n| Current `origin/dev` contains a subsequently changed/reviewed version | 183 |\n| Remote still had the old base version—truly untouched local-only paths | 0 |\n\nPR overlap explains where they went:\n\n- PR #114 overlapped **466 of the 472** local snapshot paths.\n- PRs #109, #114, and #115 together overlapped **468 of 472** paths.\n- Those overlap counts are not additive because some files were touched by multiple PRs.\n- The remaining four were:\n  - two `.conduct` artifacts intentionally excluded from a `dev` PR;\n  - two obsolete AuthFn documentation paths that were replaced/deleted remotely.\n\nAlso, the snapshot’s base is now **176 commits behind** current `origin/dev`, not merely a few commits behind. Those intervening commits include:\n\n- [PR #109](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/109): shared-package production work.\n- [PR #114](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/114): explicit integration of the local AuthFn, DataFn, FileFn, SearchFn, storage, observability, and delivery work.\n- [PR #115](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115): extensive review-driven durability, concurrency, migration, and consistency fixes.\n\nWhen the original snapshot was replayed again after those merges, only 18 files produced residual differences. Those were not silently considered integrated; they were explicitly reviewed and rejected because they included:\n\n- AuthFn dependency declarations that recreated a Turbo dependency cycle.\n- Removal of valid AuthFn workspaces.\n- Duplicate documentation blocks.\n- Invalid DataFn test syntax.\n- Duplicate idempotency and reconciliation implementations.\n- Older permission-directory behavior superseded by durable post-commit recovery.\n- An unused CLI import.\n- An older fixed-window rate-limit implementation superseded by the reviewed CAS implementation.\n\nSo the important distinction is:\n\n- **289 files:** literally integrated.\n- **165 of the other 183 files:** effectively absorbed or further evolved during reconciliation/review.\n- **18 files:** remaining local deltas deliberately not carried forward.\n- **Original worktree:** still dirty because preservation—not cleanup—was the policy.\n\nTherefore, no new `dev` PR was created in the last phase because PR #114 had already been the principal PR for those local changes, and PR #115 had already carried their review corrections. It was not because all 472 files independently appeared on remote by coincidence.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:3133-3160|note=[used the prior dirty dev provenance inventory to contextualize the local AuthFn and DataFn integration stack]\nMEMORY.md:1429-1432|note=[used the prior worktree inventory guidance and preserved dirty-worktree counts]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n019fcc94-2243-7543-81c9-399c9871de91\n019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>"}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a022b1-36ac-7732-bf2d-a946dee5da2c"}}}
