{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:05:15.001Z","ordinal":25497,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a022b5-0d75-7782-bf1e-70d04c8759ef","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"item-1453","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Likely yes for the working-tree copies, but I would not delete them blindly. I’m verifying that both dirty worktrees still match their preservation snapshots and that the snapshot refs—and the open cleanup PR branch—still exist, so we can distinguish “safe to clean” from “safe to erase every backup.”"}],"phase":"commentary"},"completed_at_ms":1787288715001}}
