{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T05:13:40.642Z","ordinal":25601,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a022bd-3622-74a1-9e3d-58463b09d9f6","call_id":"call_1jCdI9hjDReflTa9Pn3xbdFr","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7b982a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002542,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2390,\"output\":\"623-## Failures and how to do differently\\n624-\\n625:- Do not create the preservation worktree from remote `sf-next/next`; anchor it at the pre-sync local commit. Do not use broad `git add` in a mixed worktree: stage an explicit path allowlist, refetch current review threads, and use `gh pr merge --match-head-commit` after the broad gate passes. [Task 1]\\n626-\\n627-# Task Group: August 13 cross-repo SRO-728/SRO-717 reviews, PostHog, and Git workflow in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/repos\\n--\\n1021-\\n1022-# Task Group: August 11 Superfunctions audit, release, and PR work in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions\\n1023:scope: Use for exact-head security/readiness audits, authorized package publishing, or branch/worktree inventory. Keep dirty sources isolated and distinguish local gates from external CI/deployment proof.\\n1024-applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/{superfunctions,superfunctions-dev,worktrees/superfunctions/*}; reuse_rule=verify current ref, account, and package state; counts/SHA/release status are time-specific.\\n1025-\\n--\\n1043-### keywords\\n1044-\\n1045:- sf-next/next, origin/dev, publish-tag.yml, @plugfn/providers, package isolation, PR #42, gate:mcpfn-release, Node 24, MemoryFn, @rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu, --match-head-commit\\n1046-\\n1047-## Task 3: Compare local next and dev worktree state, success\\n--\\n1063-### keywords\\n1064-\\n1065:- PR #103, SF-8, `21n/report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0`, `reviewThreads`, GraphQL, Outlook SSRF, checkpoint null, Python rate limit, `0cea01c4`, `git push origin HEAD:SF-8`\\n1066-\\n1067-## User preferences\\n--\\n1077-- McpFn release gate needs Node 24; a root install can mask standalone dependencies. In hosted McpFn CI, run `node scripts/ci-install-rollup-native.mjs` after `npm ci` before the gate because npm can omit `@rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu`. Validate post-push local/ref/PR SHA equality and merge with an exact-head guard. [Task 2]\\n1078-- Worktree snapshots are cache-relative without fetch; take final counts after detailed inspection if a checkout changes concurrently. [Task 3]\\n1079:- For private Superfunctions PRs, inspect authenticated current `reviewThreads`/head comments, including `isResolved` and `isOutdated`, before editing. PR #103 used a clean isolated exact-head worktree because the existing checkout was dirty; after user authorization, fetch `origin/SF-8`, require it to equal `HEAD^`, then push `HEAD:SF-8` and verify local/remote/live PR SHA equality. [Task 4]\\n1080-\\n1081-## Failures and how to do differently\\n--\\n1083-- Passing focused PR tests missed `resolveScope()` precedence; external billing/CI gaps are separate from code correctness. [Task 1]\\n1084-- Do not dispatch all tag releases sharing one concurrency group. Remove sibling-source aliases and root-tool assumptions from package tests; do not attribute generic JavaScript, Python, Vercel, or dependency-cycle baseline failures to McpFn without the exact job logs. [Task 2]\\n1085:- A malformed GraphQL query can fail; use paginated `reviewThreads(first:100, after:$cursor)` and check `pageInfo.hasNextPage`. If `python` is absent from PATH, use the bundled runtime via a temporary `python` symlink before running `node scripts/ci-run-python-package.mjs plugfn/python`; keep full-repository baseline failures separate from changed-surface tests. [Task 4]\\n1086-\\n1087-# Task Group: August 11 btnextjs and btnextjs-two review/fix work in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/repos\\n--\\n1180-### keywords\\n1181-\\n1182:- splane, 21n/report-and-fix-pr, PR #93, BillFn, GraphQL reviewThreads, package-lock.json, Kysely, memory adapter, `gh pr merge 93 --merge`\\n1183-\\n1184-## Task 2: PR #112 ExtFn review refetch, fixes, and push, success\\n--\\n1190-### keywords\\n1191-\\n1192:- PR #112, ExtFn, reviewThreads, unresolved threads, e7b4853f, 73 tests, billing lock\\n1193-\\n1194-## Task 3: ApiFn PR #113 refetch, remediation, and ready-for-review, success\\n--\\n1200-### keywords\\n1201-\\n1202:- PR #113, ApiFn, reviewThreads, TS5055, .svelte.d.ts, gh pr ready, faea2d04, unresolvedCount:0\\n1203-\\n1204-## Task 4: Remediate Superfunctions PR #103 locally through the hosted Skillplane workflow, success\\n--\\n1210-### keywords\\n1211-\\n1212:- PR #103, 21n/report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0, SF-8-ci-fixes, reviewThreads, 46 unique findings, Ruff, mypy, PlugFn, 236 review threads, delivery claim token\\n1213-\\n1214-## Task 5: Preserve dirty `next`, sync `sf-next/next`, and remediate MDFN PR #43, success\\n--\\n1243-## Reusable knowledge\\n1244-\\n1245:- Related skill: skills/thread-aware-pr-review-triage/SKILL.md. Collect PR metadata, pagination-complete inline comments, submitted reviews, conversation comments, and GraphQL `reviewThreads` before edits; collapse threads into current valid findings and mark stale ones separately. [Task 1][Task 3][Task 6]\\n1246-- Quote `gh api` endpoint URLs containing `?` in zsh. Preview ignored generated siblings with `git clean -ndX <path>` before targeted cleanup; stale compiled JS can make Vitest exercise old code. For a large root lockfile conflict, select a coherent side then regenerate with `npm install --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts`; resolve adapter conflicts semantically and rerun focused DB/BillFn/Apple/Python gates before merging. [Task 1]\\n1247-- CI blocked by a GitHub billing/account lock is neither a passing nor a demonstrated code failure; retain it as an external verification gap. [Task 2][Task 3]\\n--\\n1250-- MDFN uses Markdown as canonical state with structured document, selection, diagnostics, history, and editorial sidecar; its framework-neutral kernel follows UIFn’s core -> DOM -> adapter-kit -> React/Svelte/Solid pattern. `npm run verify:mdfn` is the broad authoritative gate. [Task 5]\\n1251-- For Superfunctions admin inventory, inspect tracked `*fn` packages directly because the root README is incomplete. `uifn/sf` has backed panels for AuthFn, PlugFn, FileFn, and BillFn; re-inventory tracked `*fn` directories before relying on the 35-product snapshot. [Task 6]\\n1252:- PR #44 triage should fetch GraphQL `reviewThreads(first:100)` plus submitted reviews, issue comments, and inline comments, then separate current from outdated findings. The validated fixes were canonical `installationId`/deprecated `organizationId` handling, URI-encoded route-placeholder materialization in `AdminClient`, and direct-service rejection of undeclared WatchFn filters. [Task 6]\\n1253-\\n1254-## Failures and how to do differently\\n--\\n1409-- Existing Svelte/Vite/Vitest startup failed with `TypeError: Cannot convert undefined or null to object`; use Node built-in tests for the focused redirect worker and do not treat that baseline as redirect failure. [Task 1]\\n1410-\\n1411:# Task Group: Superfunctions worktree inventory in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions\\n1412-scope: Use for a read-only inventory of registered Superfunctions worktrees and local-change magnitude. Separate tracked source, untracked artifacts, disk consumption, and cache-relative remote divergence.\\n1413-applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions; reuse_rule=inventory counts and branch/upstream state are snapshots; rerun the listed commands and do not mutate unless authorized.\\n--\\n1429-## Reusable knowledge\\n1430-\\n1431:- `git worktree list --porcelain` is the authoritative registered-worktree inventory. For each worktree, use `git status --short --branch`, `git diff --shortstat`, `git diff --name-status`, `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`, and `git rev-list --left-right --count \\\"$branch...$remote\\\"`; separate tracked source, untracked artifacts, and disk consumption. [Task 1]\\n1432-- At the inspected snapshot, nine entries included eight live worktrees and one stale/prunable `/private/tmp/sf-docsfn-core-pack-a2712232`. `superfunctions-dev` was a broad dirty integration stack (377 tracked + 95 untracked paths, 10 commits behind stored `origin/dev`); `SFN-15` held large generated `.conduct` evidence; `codex/mcpfn` had 103 modified + 80 untracked paths. Counts and divergence are snapshot-specific. [Task 1]\\n1433-\\n--\\n3238-### keywords\\n3239-\\n3240:- kgqa, PR 88, service_request, raw_service_response, is_raw_service_response, service_raw_answer, reviewThreads, gh api graphql, uv run pytest\\n3241-\\n3242-## Task 2: Fix data_analyst_agent PR 125 response-contract schema locally, success\\n--\\n3267-## Reusable knowledge\\n3268-\\n3269:- For these private repos, live `reviewThreads` from authenticated `gh` / GraphQL were the source of truth; connector fetches returned `404`, so do not rely on unauthenticated PR metadata alone. [Task 1][Task 2]\\n3270-- In `kgqa`, the raw-service-response path must preserve `\\\"\\\"` as an intentional raw response; use `is_raw_service_response` directly instead of truthiness or `is None` fallbacks. [Task 1]\\n3271-- In `data_analyst_agent`, the response contract for `meeting_display_items` should mirror the parser/model boundary with nested item objects (`title`, `source_kunit_ids`, nullable `assignee_name`, `priority`) rather than bucket-level arrays only. [Task 2]\\n--\\n3276-## Failures and how to do differently\\n3277-\\n3278:- Symptom: private-repo PR fetches say `404` or repository not found. Cause: connector access is insufficient for these repos. Fix: switch quickly to authenticated `gh pr view` and GraphQL `reviewThreads` instead of burning time on connector retries. [Task 1][Task 2]\\n3279-- Symptom: a raw service response falls through to formatted/citation output. Cause: the code used raw-answer truthiness instead of the explicit `is_raw_service_response` flag. Fix: gate the whole path off the boolean flag so empty strings remain valid raw output. [Task 1]\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a022bc-f6ca-7fc3-93cb-4099d2760313","create_time":1787289220.642346}}}
