{"timestamp":"2026-08-21T06:22:21.185Z","ordinal":25865,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019febe2-4640-7603-85dc-6a0600b762b0","turn_id":"01a022fa-bdb6-76a2-ae8a-55c7d75217ca","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"item-1500","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"No—not completely.\n\nComparing the latest remote refs:\n\n- `origin/dev`: `72aabce9`\n- `sf-next/next`: `d4d4256a`\n- `dev` is an ancestor of `next`; `next` is 250 commits ahead.\n\nShared `packages/*` status, excluding `.conduct`:\n\n- **40 packages exist on both branches.**\n- **39 are fully identical.**\n- **1 common package differs:** `@superfunctions/observability`\n  - `next` adds `packages/observability/vitest.config.ts`.\n  - Both manifests remain at version `0.0.1`.\n  - The file affects testing, but is not included in the declared `files: [\"dist\"]` publish output.\n- **1 package exists only on next:** `@superfunctions/admin@0.1.0`.\n- **No shared packages exist only on dev.**\n\nSo shared code is nearly synchronized, but exact parity requires deciding whether to:\n\n1. Backport the Observability Vitest configuration to dev.\n2. Keep `@superfunctions/admin` next-only or add it to dev.\n\nAlso, the local `next` checkout itself is still 185 commits behind `sf-next/next`; release inventory should use the remote ref or a clean exact-head worktree, not that stale local checkout.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":1052,"lineEnd":1054,"note":"used prior common-scope comparison context while verifying the current refs"},{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":1068,"lineEnd":1071,"note":"used prior release scoping guidance for shared packages"}],"rolloutIds":["019ff0e2-8dd1-7782-ac67-85708209c32d"]}},"completed_at_ms":1787293341185}}
